#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""PLAN.md 2.30: the end-to-end test, against the Compose stack's own images.

It brings up postgres, bucket, ace, the parser, sandbox and network pools and the e2e profile's
responder under a project of its own (ace-rs-e2e), with:

- a signatures repository it makes under target/e2e/ from tools/ace3/trees/signatures, holding
  one rule that matches a marker string only in a file tagged type=email.attachment (its meta_tags
  directive);
- tests/e2e/site/overlay.yaml, which points the RDAP module and the proxy_domain_splunk instance
  of the Splunk module at the responder's recordings, so nothing reaches the internet;
- a 15-second lease, so a task a killed pool held comes back quickly.

It makes an API key holding alert:create with `ace user create-key` in the ace container, since the
stack has no default key (PLAN.md 5.5), and submits through the JSON API with it, as `ace compare`
does below. It checks the GUI's login page and its Datastar on the same port (PLAN.md 5.7). Then it
submits samples/ace-rs/email/e2e.email.rfc822, an email with a DKIM signing domain
(example.com) in its headers and a zip attachment holding the marker, twice. Each time, the email, archive and YARA modules run in
email mode; the YARA match on the attachment makes the root an alert in correlation mode, which
runs RDAP and the Splunk instance, the delayed module, on the domain. The email goes in with the
original_email directive, as ace3's collectors give it, so the email logger runs once the rest of the
root is done and records the email's thread in brocess with its task's end, which the thread module,
running for correlation, waits for and then reads back (PLAN.md 7.4). The second time the
parser pool is frozen before the submission, so the core leases it a task it never answers, and
it is killed with SIGKILL while it holds that lease, then started again. Both roots must have
results from all five modules and complete; the second only later. The same email goes in both
times, so their trees in the normal form (PLAN.md 3.1) must be the same text, which goes to
<work>/normal-form.json. The core's log must have one per-root metrics event (`ace_core::metrics`,
ace3's since 972058d1) for each pass each of the two completed, the last with the root's counts,
and after it one module event for each module that ran in that pass, with its tasks' run times.

Then search (PLAN.md 7.11): the indexer, a task of `ace serve`, has to have indexed both alerts once
their passes completed, embedding their text with the model the ace image carries into the pgvector
the Postgres image carries, and a search through the JSON API has to find them by their title's words,
one by its id as an exact match, nothing for a query that resembles nothing, and each as the alert
most like the other.

Then the AI investigation API (PLAN.md 7.15), which tests/e2e/site/overlay.yaml turns on with ace3's
testing backend: a key scoped to it lists the backend, runs a query that answers its canned rows,
reads the first alert and finds it by its id, and is refused by the main API; each of those wrote its
audit row, and the query was counted by the limiter in Postgres. Nothing leaves the stack: the backend
reaches nothing, and ACE calls no model.

Then the browser test (PLAN.md 5.8, 5.9 and 5.10): the e2e profile's headless Chromium, pinned by digest in
compose.yaml, logs in to the GUI as an analyst that `ace user create-first` makes and opens a third
submission's alert page while the network pool is frozen, so the page has no RDAP result. The pool is
let go, and the RDAP result has to appear on the open page, pushed by its live stream, with no reload
and nothing the page's Content-Security-Policy refused. The page it watches is the alert's whole
tree: the alert page starts at the branches that carry a detection, which the test checks first, and
the RDAP result lands on an observable with none. Then a second analyst takes that alert in a session
of their own, and the open page has to say that its ownership changed and to whom, pushed by the same
stream (the owner's decision of 2026-11-15). Then it opens the alert list (5.10) filtered to
open alerts, which shows that alert, and a filter that matches nothing, which lists nothing; it opens
the open alerts again, dispositions the alert through the JSON API with a key of its own, and the
list's refresh has to drop it from the open page, again with no reload and nothing refused. Then it
ticks ranges of alerts on a list of eight it makes (ace3 5fb36276): shift+click, a drag over the boxes
and Shift+Space, sent as the browser's own mouse and key events, across two refreshes of the list, and
Set Disposition on what is ticked (`check_range_selection`). It drives
the browser over the DevTools protocol, with a WebSocket client here, so it needs nothing more than
python3. Before the list, it opens that alert's relationship graph (5.13) from the alert page's link and
checks that vis.js drew a node for the alert and each of its observables, results and tags, with nothing
refused and nothing thrown.

It also runs a GUI command (PLAN.md 5.12): signed in as that analyst, it starts `ace --help` and `ace serve`
through the JSON API with the session, which the parser pool runs contained, and checks that the help
completed with ace's usage and that `serve` was refused, as a command a contained process can't run.

Then the analyst-edited lists (PLAN.md 5.14): signed in as that analyst, it enables the email's sender for
detection on the observable_detection list through the JSON API and submits the email once more, with
nothing restarted. The sender has to be found enabled for detection, the root has to alert, and the
entry's audit row has to name the analyst. It deletes the entry the same way before anything else runs,
so the comparison below sees the empty lists ace3's trees were made with. Before the comparison it
gives ace-rs what make-trees gave ace3's tagging and detection modules (PLAN.md 7.6): the observables
enabled for detection in tools/ace3/trees/detections.json, added through the detection API with a key
holding detection:write, and the tags of tools/ace3/trees/observable_tags.json, with SQL; the site
tagger's rows are in the overlay.

Then the scanners (PLAN.md 7.7): it builds ace-rs-js-deobfuscator and ace-rs-phishkit from ace3's checkout
with docker/scanners/build when this host hasn't them, and the stack's scanner pool runs them, phishkit's
on the e2e profile's internal network, `scanned`. It submits samples/ace-rs/web/phishkit_page.html as an
email's attachment named phishkit_page.htm, the one extension tests/e2e/site/overlay.yaml lets phishkit render, in correlation mode, and phishkit_analyzer has to render it and javascript_deobfuscation
run the script html_js_extraction writes out of it, each through a scan the queue held while its task
waited. Then it submits the page again and dispositions the root while its phishkit scan runs, and the
pool has to kill the scanner and remove its container; and again, and kills the pool with SIGKILL while
the scanner runs, and the pool has to remove the container it left when it starts again, while the core
ends the scan abandoned once its lease runs out and the module says so. ace3's scanner managers, and any
container they started, have to be as they were.

Then the library diff's self-test runs (PLAN.md 4.8), and tools/ace3/modules/check checks the module
inventory, docs/modules.md, against ace3's config at the head of ace3's checkout (PLAN.md 7.1), and its
modules that read ACE's own data against ace3's code, each with what serves it (7.2), and its modules
that start a process, each with a decision for every program (7.3); under CI, which has no ace3
checkout, that check is skipped.

It then runs `ace compare` (PLAN.md 3.3, crates/ace-app/src/compare.rs) over the sample set, each
sample in the cli mode against ace3's tree in tools/ace3/trees/reference/ (3.2), and writes the
report to <work>/compare/. It enforces the acceptance threshold in docs/acceptance.md: a difference
in any sample that tools/ace3/trees/differences.md doesn't list fails the test, and so does a row
that matches nothing, so the list stays true. So does a sample absent from this machine, unless CI
is set: CI doesn't have the git-ignored samples/local/, so there it holds over the tracked samples,
and the report says how many were absent.

Last, the analysis cache's two-run check (PLAN.md decision 26, docs/decisions/0004): everything above
runs with the cache off, which tests/e2e/site/overlay.yaml says, and this restarts the core with a copy
of the site directory whose overlay turns it on, then submits CACHE_SAMPLES twice, as `ace compare`
submits a sample. They reach each cacheable module the stack runs on a sample (qrcode, pdf_link_text,
rdap_analyzer, nrd_analyzer and site_tagger; ocr runs on none). Every result the first run kept (each
one without an error) has to come from the cache the second time, with its `cached_at`, and no task of
it may run in a pool; what the first run couldn't keep runs again; and each sample's tree in the normal
form has to be the same both times wherever two runs with the cache off agree: a control run with the
cache off, before, says where they don't (ExifTool's file times, Ghostscript's rewrite of a PDF, whose
bytes and so sha256 change every run), and files are named by their paths for the comparison, since
their sha256s are what changes. A kept result on such a file misses, since its bytes are new, and so
does a value chosen by such a file's sha256, as a redirection to one of two files. With the cache still
on, the scanner check's page is rendered twice: phishkit_analyzer's first result has to be kept under
its scan's image id, and the second root has to take it from the cache, with the same files and no
scan of its own (PLAN.md decision 27). Then the core goes back to the site's own overlay.

Usage: tests/e2e/run [--keep] [--no-build] [--compare] [--jobs N] [--only CHECKS]
                     [--samples GLOBS | --modules NAMES | --crates NAMES | --changed]
  --keep      leaves the stack up
  --no-build  starts the stack from the images this host has, without building them
  --compare   only brings up the stack and runs `ace compare` over the sample set, reporting
              differences without enforcing the threshold, and fails only when a sample can't be
              run
  --jobs N    `ace compare` has N samples in the stack at once; 1 runs them one at a time
              (crates/ace-app/src/compare.rs, *Several samples at once*). Without it, as many as
              the parser pool has slots here: 8 on a machine whose Docker has 10 CPUs or more,
              4 on a small one
  --only CHECKS
              runs only these checks, comma-separated, of: gui, command, email, search, ai, lists,
              scanners, browser, library-diff, inventory, compare, cache. search and ai need email's
              roots and cache needs compare's world, so each brings in the other. `none` runs no
              check: the stack comes up, with its key and ruleset, and with --keep stays up
  --samples GLOBS, --modules NAMES, --crates NAMES, --changed
              compare only some of the sample set, which is then the only check, or the one
              --only adds to its own:
              the samples whose paths match a glob; those where ace3's tree has a result of one of
              the modules, or where the last report (<work>/compare/report.json) found a
              difference in one; the modules docs/modules.md says a crate holds; or the crates
              with uncommitted changes in this checkout, all of the sample set when one of them is
              a crate other than a module's, and none when no crate changed. The threshold then
              holds over the samples compared: no unexplained difference, no failed sample and,
              outside CI, no absent one. A row of differences.md that matched nothing isn't
              checked, since the samples it covers may not have run.

A change is checked in full, with every check and the whole sample set, by a run without --only or
a selection of samples, which is what `make test-all` runs.

With ACE_RS_TAKES_AUDIT=1 in the environment, the stack's core audits the modules' declarations of what
they take rather than applying them (PLAN.md decision 23): it queues every task and marks the ones a
declaration declines. After the comparison the test then fails if a marked task stored a result or
failed, and writes the marked tasks by module to <work>/takes-audit.txt.

Exits 0 when every check passes. Needs docker compose and python3 on the host.

A site repository runs the same scenario against its own images (PLAN.md 2.32) by setting:

- ACE_RS_E2E_COMPOSE: its Compose file, whose services have this file's names (postgres, bucket,
  ace, ai, parsers, sandbox, lookups, scanners and the e2e profile's responder, and its browser
  for the browser test), with the `scanned` network, and whose ace and ai services get their
  database logins in ACE_RS_DATABASE_URL;
- ACE_RS_E2E_PREFIX: the prefix of that file's variables, such as SITE_ACE_RS_, in place of ACE_RS_;
- ACE_RS_E2E_PROJECT: the Compose project the test runs under, in place of ace-rs-e2e;
- ACE_RS_E2E_SITE: the site overlay directory, in place of tests/e2e/site;
- ACE_RS_E2E_WORK: where the signatures repository goes, in place of target/e2e;
- ACE_RS_E2E_PORT: the host port, as for ace-rs;
- ACE_RS_E2E_ACE_COMMAND: the ace service's binary, in place of ace;
- ACE_RS_E2E_COMPARE: 1 to run the comparison with ace3 and its threshold as well;
- ACE_RS_E2E_CACHE: 1 to run the analysis cache's two-run check as well, which needs
  ACE_RS_E2E_COMPARE, since it runs in the world the comparison sets up.

A site's own modules may differ from ace3's by design, so setting ACE_RS_E2E_SITE skips the
comparison, unless ACE_RS_E2E_COMPARE is 1: a site whose binaries hold every module of ace-rs's, and
whose own modules run on nothing in the sample set, has to make the same trees. Its overlay then
needs what tests/e2e/site/overlay.yaml gives ace-rs. The cache's two-run check is skipped too, unless
ACE_RS_E2E_CACHE is 1: a site whose binaries hold ace-rs's cacheable modules has to keep and reuse their
results as ace-rs's do. Its overlay then turns the cache off and has a site_tagger section, as ace-rs's
does, and the check fails for any of ace-rs's cacheable modules that took nothing from the cache. The library diff's self-test and the module
inventory check this repository, not a stack, so a site's run never includes them.
"""

import base64
import fnmatch
import hashlib
import http.client
import json
import os
import re
import shutil
import socket
import struct
import subprocess
import sys
import time
import urllib.parse
import urllib.request
import uuid
from pathlib import Path

ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent.parent
COMPOSE_FILE = Path(os.environ.get("ACE_RS_E2E_COMPOSE", ROOT / "compose.yaml")).resolve()
PREFIX = os.environ.get("ACE_RS_E2E_PREFIX", "ACE_RS_")
WORK = Path(os.environ.get("ACE_RS_E2E_WORK", ROOT / "target" / "e2e")).resolve()
SITE = Path(os.environ.get("ACE_RS_E2E_SITE", ROOT / "tests" / "e2e" / "site")).resolve()
PROJECT = os.environ.get("ACE_RS_E2E_PROJECT", "ace-rs-e2e")
PORT = os.environ.get("ACE_RS_E2E_PORT", "7444")
ACE_COMMAND = os.environ.get("ACE_RS_E2E_ACE_COMMAND", "ace")
# A site's run: against another repository's Compose file and overlay.
SITE_RUN = "ACE_RS_E2E_SITE" in os.environ
COMPARE = not SITE_RUN or os.environ.get("ACE_RS_E2E_COMPARE") == "1"
CACHE = not SITE_RUN or os.environ.get("ACE_RS_E2E_CACHE") == "1"
LEASE_SECONDS = 15


def pool_slots():
    """How many tasks the parser and sandbox pools run at once here: Docker's CPUs less two, for the
    core and Postgres, and no fewer than the stack's own 4 or more than 8. The comparison is bound by
    these pools: at 4 they are full while the machine is a third used
    (docs/measurements/compare-speed.md)."""
    cpus = subprocess.run(
        ["docker", "info", "--format", "{{.NCPU}}"], capture_output=True, text=True, check=False
    ).stdout.strip()
    return min(8, max(4, int(cpus) - 2)) if cpus.isdigit() else 4


POOL_SLOTS = pool_slots()
RULE = "ace_rs_e2e_attachment"
SAMPLE = "ace-rs/email/e2e.email.rfc822"
EMAIL_SAMPLE = ROOT / "samples" / SAMPLE
TREES = ROOT / "tools" / "ace3" / "trees"
MODULES = [
    "email_analyzer",
    "archive",
    "yara_scanner_v3_4",
    "rdap_analyzer",
    "proxy_domain_splunk",
]

ENV = {
    **os.environ,
    **{
        PREFIX + name: value
        for name, value in {
            "STACK": PROJECT,
            "PORT_HTTPS": PORT,
            "SITE": str(SITE),
            # `ace serve-ai` reads an overlay of its own (PLAN.md 7.15)
            "AI_OVERLAY": str(SITE / "ai.yaml"),
            "SIGNATURES": str(WORK / "signatures"),
            "LEASE_SECONDS": str(LEASE_SECONDS),
            "RULESET_POLL_SECONDS": "2",
            "POOL_RULESET_POLL_SECONDS": "2",
            # the recorded Splunk takes any password
            "SPLUNK_PASSWORD": "ace-rs-fake-password",
            # the pools that run a process per task, sized to this machine unless the environment
            # says, with the stack's 1 GiB of memory limit a slot
            **{
                name: os.environ.get(PREFIX + name, value)
                for name, value in {
                    "PARSERS_CONCURRENCY": str(POOL_SLOTS),
                    "SANDBOX_CONCURRENCY": str(POOL_SLOTS),
                    "PARSERS_MEM_LIMIT": f"{POOL_SLOTS}g",
                    "SANDBOX_MEM_LIMIT": f"{POOL_SLOTS}g",
                }.items()
            },
            # phishkit's containers go on the e2e profile's internal network, which reaches the
            # responder and nothing outside the stack (compose.yaml's `scanned`)
            "PHISHKIT_NETWORK": f"{PROJECT}_scanned",
        }.items()
    },
}
ENV.pop("COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME", None)
COMPOSE = ["docker", "compose", "-f", str(COMPOSE_FILE), "--profile", "e2e"]
SERVICES = ["postgres", "bucket", "ace", "ai", "parsers", "sandbox", "lookups", "scanners", "responder"]
# PLAN.md 7.7: the page the scanner checks render, and its inline script the deobfuscator runs
SCANNER_PAGE = ROOT / "samples" / "ace-rs" / "web" / "phishkit_page.html"
SCANNER_IMAGES = ["ace-rs-js-deobfuscator:latest", "ace-rs-phishkit:latest"]
# The analyst the browser test logs in as, and the GUI as the browser reaches it on the stack's network.
ANALYST = "e2e-analyst"
ANALYST_PASSWORD = "e2e analyst password, not a secret"
# A second analyst, who takes an alert the first has open (the ownership-changed notice).
SECOND_ANALYST = "e2e-analyst-two"
SECOND_ANALYST_PASSWORD = "e2e second analyst password, not a secret"
GUI_IN_STACK = "http://ace:8000"
# Ports of Python libraries: each must have results from both systems, because a comparison with
# nothing compared passes.
LIBRARY_PORTS = [
    "msoffice_encryption_analyzer", "olevba_v1_2", "pcodedmp", "pdf_analyzer", "rtfole",
    "xlmdeobfuscator",
]


def log(message):
    print(f"e2e: {message}", flush=True)


def compose(*args, check=True, capture=False, exit_code=False):
    result = subprocess.run(
        [*COMPOSE, *args], env=ENV, cwd=COMPOSE_FILE.parent, text=True, capture_output=capture
    )
    if exit_code:
        return result.returncode
    if check and result.returncode != 0:
        raise SystemExit(
            f"e2e: docker compose {' '.join(args)} failed ({result.returncode})\n"
            f"{result.stderr if capture else ''}"
        )
    return result.stdout if capture else ""


def database_login(service):
    """The database URL the Compose file gives a service, and the login in it: ace-rs's own names, or
    a site's."""
    config = json.loads(compose("config", "--format", "json", capture=True))
    url = config["services"][service]["environment"]["ACE_RS_DATABASE_URL"]
    return url, urllib.parse.urlsplit(url).username


def sql(query):
    """Rows of a query against the stack's Postgres, as lists of strings."""
    # the database and user the stack's Compose file gave the postgres service
    out = compose(
        "exec", "-T", "-e", f"QUERY={query}", "postgres", "sh", "-c",
        'psql -U "$POSTGRES_USER" -d "$POSTGRES_DB" -At -F "\t" -v ON_ERROR_STOP=1 -c "$QUERY"',
        capture=True,
    )
    return [line.split("\t") for line in out.splitlines() if line]


def git(*args):
    subprocess.run(
        ["git", "-C", str(WORK / "signatures"), "-c", "user.name=ace-rs e2e",
         "-c", "user.email=e2e@example.invalid", "-c", "commit.gpgsign=false",
         "-c", "init.defaultBranch=main", *args],
        check=True, capture_output=True,
    )


def make_signatures():
    """A repository with tools/ace3/trees/signatures' one fixture rule, the rule ace3's trees
    scanned with, committed. Returns its commit."""
    repo = WORK / "signatures"
    shutil.rmtree(repo, ignore_errors=True)
    shutil.copytree(ROOT / "tools" / "ace3" / "trees" / "signatures", repo / "yara")
    git("init", "-q")
    git("add", ".")
    git("commit", "-q", "-m", "the end-to-end test's rule")
    return subprocess.run(
        ["git", "-C", str(repo), "rev-parse", "HEAD"], check=True, capture_output=True,
        text=True,
    ).stdout.strip()


def make_key():
    """An API key that can submit, made in the ace container, which holds the database. The key goes
    to `ace compare` through ACE_RS_API_KEY in this process's environment, not its command line."""
    out = compose(
        "exec", "-T", "ace", ACE_COMMAND, "user", "create-key", "e2e-submitter",
        "--grant", "alert:create", capture=True,
    )
    token = next(
        (line.split(": ", 1)[1] for line in out.splitlines()
         if line.startswith("token (shown once): ")),
        None,
    )
    if not token:
        raise SystemExit(f"e2e: `ace user create-key` printed no token:\n{out}")
    ENV["ACE_RS_API_KEY"] = token
    return token


def submit(email, mode="email", observables=()):
    """Submits a root, with the email as its file if there is one, and returns its uuid."""
    boundary = f"ace-rs-e2e-{uuid.uuid4().hex}"
    analysis = json.dumps({
        "description": "ace-rs end-to-end test",
        "analysis_mode": mode,
        "observables": list(observables),
    })
    body = (
        f"--{boundary}\r\nContent-Disposition: form-data; name=\"analysis\"\r\n\r\n"
        f"{analysis}\r\n"
    ).encode()
    if email is not None:
        body += (
            f"--{boundary}\r\nContent-Disposition: form-data; name=\"file\"; "
            f"filename=\"email.rfc822\"\r\nContent-Type: message/rfc822\r\n\r\n"
        ).encode() + email + b"\r\n"
    body += f"--{boundary}--\r\n".encode()
    request = urllib.request.Request(
        f"http://127.0.0.1:{PORT}/api/analysis/v1/submit",
        data=body,
        method="POST",
        headers={
            "Authorization": f"Bearer {ENV['ACE_RS_API_KEY']}",
            "Content-Type": f"multipart/form-data; boundary={boundary}",
        },
    )
    with urllib.request.urlopen(request, timeout=30) as response:
        if response.status != 201:
            raise SystemExit(f"e2e: the submission answered {response.status}")
        return json.load(response)["id"]


def submit_file(data, name, mode, yara_meta=()):
    """Submits a root with one file at `name`, with these yara_meta tags, and returns its uuid."""
    boundary = f"ace-rs-e2e-{uuid.uuid4().hex}"
    analysis = json.dumps({
        "description": "ace-rs end-to-end test",
        "analysis_mode": mode,
        "file_yara_meta": {name: list(yara_meta)},
    })
    body = (
        f"--{boundary}\r\nContent-Disposition: form-data; name=\"analysis\"\r\n\r\n{analysis}\r\n"
        f"--{boundary}\r\nContent-Disposition: form-data; name=\"file\"; filename=\"{name}\"\r\n"
        f"Content-Type: application/octet-stream\r\n\r\n"
    ).encode() + data + f"\r\n--{boundary}--\r\n".encode()
    request = urllib.request.Request(
        f"http://127.0.0.1:{PORT}/api/analysis/v1/submit", data=body, method="POST",
        headers={"Authorization": f"Bearer {ENV['ACE_RS_API_KEY']}",
                 "Content-Type": f"multipart/form-data; boundary={boundary}"},
    )
    with urllib.request.urlopen(request, timeout=30) as response:
        if response.status != 201:
            raise SystemExit(f"e2e: the submission answered {response.status}")
        return json.load(response)["id"]


def build_scanner_images():
    """The scanner images (PLAN.md 7.7), built from ace3's checkout by docker/scanners/build when this
    host hasn't them. Without a checkout, as under CI, the test can't build them, and says so."""
    missing = [image for image in SCANNER_IMAGES if subprocess.run(
        ["docker", "image", "inspect", image], capture_output=True).returncode != 0]
    if not missing:
        return
    log(f"building the scanner images {missing} from ace3's sources")
    names = [image.removeprefix("ace-rs-").removesuffix(":latest") for image in missing]
    if subprocess.run([str(ROOT / "docker" / "scanners" / "build"), *names]).returncode != 0:
        raise SystemExit("e2e: docker/scanners/build failed; the scanner pool needs its images")


def scanner_containers(*labels):
    """The ids of the containers on this host's daemon with every one of `labels`, running or not."""
    out = subprocess.run(
        ["docker", "ps", "-a", "-q", *[a for label in labels for a in ("--filter", f"label={label}")]],
        capture_output=True, text=True, check=True,
    ).stdout
    return [line for line in out.split() if line]


def ace3_scanner_state():
    """ace3's scanner managers and the scanners they run, which nothing here may touch."""
    out = subprocess.run(
        ["docker", "ps", "-a", "--format", "{{.ID}} {{.Names}} {{.State}}",
         "--filter", "label=com.docker.compose.project=ace"],
        capture_output=True, text=True, check=True,
    ).stdout
    managers = sorted(line for line in out.splitlines() if "phishkit" in line or "deobfuscator" in line)
    return managers, scanner_containers("phishkit.job_id")


def running_scan(root, within=120):
    """The id of the root's phishkit scan once its pool has started its container, and the container."""
    def found():
        rows = sql(f"""SELECT id FROM queue.scans WHERE root_id = '{root}' AND scanner = 'phishkit'
                       AND state = 'running'""")
        if not rows:
            return None
        containers = scanner_containers(f"ace-rs.scanner.stack={PROJECT}", f"ace-rs.scanner.scan={rows[0][0]}")
        return (rows[0][0], containers[0]) if containers else None
    return wait_for(f"root {root}'s phishkit scan to start its container", found, within=within)


def check_scanners(failures):
    """PLAN.md 7.7's Done check: phishkit_analyzer and javascript_deobfuscation results come through
    the queue, from scans the scanner pool ran in ace3's scanner images; a cancelled root's scanner is
    killed and its container removed; a scanner a crashed pool left is removed when the pool starts
    again, and its scan ends abandoned; and nothing of ace3's is touched."""

    def expect(ok, message):
        log(("ok    " if ok else "FAIL  ") + message)
        if not ok:
            failures.append(message)

    ace3_before = ace3_scanner_state()
    page = SCANNER_PAGE.read_bytes()
    # an email's HTML attachment in correlation mode, which phishkit renders, and whose inline script
    # html_js_extraction writes out for the deobfuscator
    root = submit_file(page, "phishkit_page.htm", "correlation", ["type=email.attachment"])
    wait_for(f"root {root} to finish", lambda: completed_after(root) is not None, within=240)
    phishkit = sql(
        f"""SELECT r.details->>'scan_type', r.details->>'exit_code', coalesce(r.error, ''),
                   jsonb_array_length(r.details->'output_files'), r.summary
            FROM analysis.results r WHERE r.root_id = '{root}' AND r.module = 'phishkit_analyzer'"""
    )
    expect(len(phishkit) == 1 and phishkit[0][:3] == ["file", "0", ""] and int(phishkit[0][3]) >= 2,
           f"phishkit_analyzer rendered the page in its scanner: {phishkit}")
    files = sql(
        f"""SELECT f.path FROM analysis.files f WHERE f.root_id = '{root}' AND f.path LIKE 'phishkit/%'"""
    )
    expect(any(row[0].endswith("/screenshot.png") for row in files),
           f"its screenshot is a file in the alert: {[row[0] for row in files]}")
    deobfuscated = sql(
        f"""SELECT f.path, r.details->>'event_count', r.details->>'exit_code'
            FROM analysis.results r JOIN analysis.files f
              ON f.root_id = r.root_id AND f.observable_id = r.observable_id
            WHERE r.root_id = '{root}' AND r.module = 'javascript_deobfuscation'"""
    )
    expect(any(row[2] == "0" and row[1] not in ("0", None) for row in deobfuscated),
           f"javascript_deobfuscation ran the page's script in its scanner: {deobfuscated}")
    trace = sql(
        f"""SELECT f.path FROM analysis.files f WHERE f.root_id = '{root}'
            AND f.path LIKE '%deobfuscated-%'"""
    )
    expect(bool(trace), f"the deobfuscator's trace is a file in the alert: {trace}")
    scans = sql(f"SELECT scanner, state::text FROM queue.scans WHERE root_id = '{root}' ORDER BY id")
    expect(sorted(scans) == [["js-deobfuscator", "completed"], ["phishkit", "completed"]],
           f"the root's two scans ran through the queue and completed: {scans}")
    left = scanner_containers(f"ace-rs.scanner.stack={PROJECT}")
    expect(not left, f"no scanner container is left: {left}")

    # cancelled while its scanner runs: the pool kills it at its next renewal and removes it
    root = submit_file(page, "phishkit_page.htm", "correlation", ["type=email.attachment"])
    scan, container = running_scan(root)
    # dispositioning a root cancels its analysis (ace_service::Service::disposition)
    out = compose(
        "exec", "-T", "ace", ACE_COMMAND, "user", "create-key", "e2e-scan-canceller",
        "--grant", "alert:write", capture=True,
    )
    token = next((line.split(": ", 1)[1] for line in out.splitlines()
                  if line.startswith("token (shown once): ")), None)
    request = urllib.request.Request(
        f"http://127.0.0.1:{PORT}/api/alerts/v1/alerts/{root}/disposition",
        data=json.dumps({"disposition": "FALSE_POSITIVE"}).encode(), method="PUT",
        headers={"Authorization": f"Bearer {token}", "Content-Type": "application/json"},
    )
    with urllib.request.urlopen(request, timeout=30) as response:
        expect(response.status == 200, f"the scanned root was dispositioned: {response.status}")
    state = wait_for(f"scan {scan} to end", lambda: (sql(
        f"SELECT state::text FROM queue.scans WHERE id = {scan} AND state <> 'running'") or [[None]])[0][0],
        within=60)
    gone = wait_for(f"container {container} to go", lambda: not scanner_containers(
        f"ace-rs.scanner.scan={scan}", f"ace-rs.scanner.stack={PROJECT}") or None, within=30)
    expect(state == "cancelled" and gone, f"a cancelled root's scanner was killed and removed: {state}")

    # the pool dies with SIGKILL while its scanner runs: the scanner outlives it, and the pool removes
    # it when it starts again; the core ends the scan abandoned when its lease runs out
    root = submit_file(page, "phishkit_page.htm", "correlation", ["type=email.attachment"])
    scan, container = running_scan(root)
    compose("kill", "-s", "SIGKILL", "scanners")
    survived = bool(scanner_containers(f"ace-rs.scanner.scan={scan}", f"ace-rs.scanner.stack={PROJECT}"))
    compose("start", "scanners")
    gone = wait_for(f"the restarted pool to remove container {container}", lambda: not scanner_containers(
        f"ace-rs.scanner.scan={scan}", f"ace-rs.scanner.stack={PROJECT}") or None, within=60)
    expect(survived and gone, "a scanner the killed pool left was removed when the pool started again")
    wait_for(f"root {root} to finish", lambda: completed_after(root) is not None, within=240)
    abandoned = sql(f"SELECT state::text, error FROM queue.scans WHERE id = {scan}")
    error = sql(
        f"""SELECT r.error FROM analysis.results r
            WHERE r.root_id = '{root}' AND r.module = 'phishkit_analyzer'"""
    )
    expect(abandoned and abandoned[0][0] == "abandoned"
           and bool(error) and "its pool stopped reporting on it" in (error[0][0] or ""),
           f"its scan ended abandoned, and the module says so: {abandoned} {error}")
    ace3_after = ace3_scanner_state()
    expect(ace3_after == ace3_before, f"ace3's scanner managers and scanners are as they were: {ace3_after}")


def check_gui(failures):
    """PLAN.md 5.7: `ace serve` serves the GUI on the JSON API's listener, with its security headers,
    and Datastar from the binary under a hashed name."""
    url = f"http://127.0.0.1:{PORT}"
    with urllib.request.urlopen(f"{url}/login", timeout=30) as response:
        page = response.read().decode()
        policy = response.headers.get("Content-Security-Policy", "")
    script = re.search(r'src="(/static/datastar-1\.0\.4\.[0-9a-f]{16}\.js)"', page)
    if "script-src 'self' 'nonce-" not in policy or script is None:
        log("FAIL  the GUI's login page isn't served with its policy and Datastar")
        failures.append("ace serve doesn't serve the GUI")
        return
    with urllib.request.urlopen(f"{url}{script.group(1)}", timeout=30) as response:
        digest = hashlib.sha256(response.read()).hexdigest()
    if digest != "727844adfc825ee651fb93c544a2a739986f9a21820a94524b35f0cac470cf91":
        log(f"FAIL  the GUI serves a Datastar with SHA-256 {digest}")
        failures.append("the GUI's Datastar isn't the vendored release")
        return
    log("ok    the GUI serves its login page and the vendored Datastar")


def wait_for(what, check, within, every=0.25):
    started = time.monotonic()
    while True:
        value = check()
        if value:
            return value
        if time.monotonic() - started > within:
            raise SystemExit(f"e2e: timed out after {within}s waiting for {what}")
        time.sleep(every)


def completed_after(root):
    """Seconds from the root's creation to its first completion, or None."""
    rows = sql(
        f"""SELECT extract(epoch FROM c.completed_at - r.created_at)
            FROM queue.root_completions c JOIN analysis.roots r ON r.id = c.root_id
            WHERE c.root_id = '{root}' ORDER BY c.pass LIMIT 1"""
    )
    return float(rows[0][0]) if rows else None


def tasks(root):
    return sql(
        f"""SELECT t.module, o.type, coalesce(f.path, o.value), t.state::text, t.attempts,
                   coalesce(t.error, '')
            FROM queue.tasks t JOIN analysis.observables o ON o.id = t.observable_id
            LEFT JOIN analysis.files f ON f.observable_id = o.id
            WHERE t.root_id = '{root}' ORDER BY t.id"""
    )


def check_root(root, failures):
    """Checks one root once it completed, adding a line to failures for each check that fails."""

    def expect(ok, message):
        log(("ok    " if ok else "FAIL  ") + message)
        if not ok:
            failures.append(f"{root}: {message}")

    modules = {row[0] for row in sql(
        f"SELECT DISTINCT module FROM analysis.results WHERE root_id = '{root}'"
    )}
    for module in MODULES:
        expect(module in modules, f"{module} has a result")
    mode, alerted, passes = sql(
        f"""SELECT analysis_mode, alerted_at IS NOT NULL, completed_pass = pass
            FROM analysis.roots WHERE id = '{root}'"""
    )[0]
    expect(mode == "correlation" and alerted == "t", "the YARA match made the root an alert")
    expect(passes == "t", "the root's pass completed")
    active = sql(
        f"""SELECT count(*) FROM queue.tasks WHERE root_id = '{root}'
            AND state IN ('queued', 'delayed', 'running')"""
    )[0][0]
    expect(active == "0", "no task is left queued, delayed or running")

    # the rule matched the attachment and not the extracted file, which holds the same marker;
    # a scan that matched nothing ends done with no result
    scans = {row[0]: (row[1], row[2] == "t") for row in sql(
        f"""SELECT f.path, t.state::text, coalesce(r.details::text LIKE '%{RULE}%', false)
            FROM queue.tasks t
            JOIN analysis.files f ON f.observable_id = t.observable_id AND f.root_id = t.root_id
            LEFT JOIN analysis.results r ON r.root_id = t.root_id
              AND r.observable_id = t.observable_id AND r.module = t.module
            WHERE t.root_id = '{root}' AND t.module = 'yara_scanner_v3_4'"""
    )}
    attachment = {p: v for p, v in scans.items() if p.endswith("invoice.zip")}
    extracted = {p: v for p, v in scans.items() if p.endswith("invoice.txt")}
    expect(bool(attachment) and all(v == ("done", True) for v in attachment.values()),
           f"the rule matched the tagged attachment: {attachment}")
    expect(bool(extracted) and all(v == ("done", False) for v in extracted.values()),
           f"the rule didn't match the untagged extracted file, which has the marker: "
           f"{extracted}")
    others = [p for p, v in scans.items() if v[1] and p not in attachment]
    expect(not others, f"the rule matched nothing else: {others}")

    rdap = sql(
        f"""SELECT o.value, r.details->>'lookup_protocol', coalesce(r.error, '')
            FROM analysis.results r JOIN analysis.observables o ON o.id = r.observable_id
            WHERE r.root_id = '{root}' AND r.module = 'rdap_analyzer'"""
    )
    expect(["example.com", "rdap", ""] in rdap,
           f"RDAP answered for example.com from the recording: {rdap}")
    splunk = sql(
        f"""SELECT o.value, coalesce(r.error, ''), t.attempts
            FROM analysis.results r JOIN analysis.observables o ON o.id = r.observable_id
            JOIN queue.tasks t ON t.root_id = r.root_id AND t.observable_id = r.observable_id
              AND t.module = r.module
            WHERE r.root_id = '{root}' AND r.module = 'proxy_domain_splunk'"""
    )
    expect(any(row[0] == "example.com" and row[1] == "" for row in splunk),
           f"the Splunk instance answered for example.com: {splunk}")
    delays = sql(
        f"""SELECT count(*) FROM queue.tasks
            WHERE root_id = '{root}' AND module = 'proxy_domain_splunk'
            AND first_delayed_at IS NOT NULL"""
    )[0][0]
    expect(delays != "0", "the Splunk task was delayed before its result")

    # PLAN.md 7.4: the email logger ran on the original email once the rest of the root was done,
    # stored no result, and its write landed with its task's end: the email is in brocess's thread
    # store, once however many roots it came in
    logger = sql(
        f"""SELECT t.state::text, (SELECT count(*) FROM analysis.results r
                                   WHERE r.root_id = t.root_id AND r.module = t.module)
            FROM queue.tasks t WHERE t.root_id = '{root}' AND t.module = 'email_logger'"""
    )
    expect(logger == [["done", "0"]], f"the email logger ran and stored no result: {logger}")
    message_id = re.search(rb"^Message-ID:\s*(<[^>]+>)", EMAIL_SAMPLE.read_bytes(), re.I | re.M)
    recorded = sql(
        f"""SELECT count(*) FROM brocess.email_thread_message
            WHERE message_id = '{message_id.group(1).decode()}'"""
    ) if message_id else [["none"]]
    expect(recorded == [["1"]], f"the email logger recorded the email's thread once: {recorded}")
    # and the thread module, which runs for correlation, waited for that record and found the email
    # in it, as ace3's does after its email-mode pass
    thread = sql(
        f"""SELECT o.value, jsonb_array_length(r.details->'messages')
            FROM analysis.results r JOIN analysis.observables o ON o.id = r.observable_id
            WHERE r.root_id = '{root}' AND r.module = 'email_thread_analyzer'"""
    )
    expect(thread == [[message_id.group(1).decode() if message_id else "", "1"]],
           f"the thread module laid out the recorded conversation: {thread}")


def normal_form(root):
    """The root's tree in the normal form, as text."""
    return compose("exec", "-T", "ace", ACE_COMMAND, "root", "normal-form", root, capture=True)


def check_normal_form(text, failures):
    """Checks what the form of a root from this test has to say."""

    def expect(ok, message):
        log(("ok    " if ok else "FAIL  ") + message)
        if not ok:
            failures.append(f"the normal form: {message}")

    form = json.loads(text)
    observables = form["observables"]
    modules = {m for o in observables.values() for m in o["results"]}
    expect(modules >= set(MODULES), f"it has results from all five modules: {sorted(modules)}")
    expect(text == json.dumps(form, indent=2, sort_keys=True, ensure_ascii=False) + "\n",
           "its text is what Python's json.dumps writes, so ace3's script can write the same")
    paths = {p: tags for o in observables.values() for p, tags in o.get("paths", {}).items()}
    expect(paths.get("email.rfc822") is not None and any(
        p.endswith("invoice.zip") and "type=email.attachment" in tags for p, tags in paths.items()
    ), f"files keep their paths and yara_meta tags: {sorted(paths)}")
    extracted = [o for o in observables.values()
                 if any(p.endswith("invoice.txt") for p in o.get("paths", {}))]
    expect(len(extracted) == 1 and any(
        r.startswith("extracted_from file:") for r in extracted[0]["relationships"]
    ), "the extracted file says what it was extracted from")
    expect(any(RULE in json.dumps(o["detections"]) or o["detections"]
               for o in observables.values()), "the YARA match's detection is on an observable")
    expect(not re.search(r'"/(tmp|var|opt|home|root|usr|workspace)/', text),
           "it holds no absolute path")
    expect(not re.search(r'"(created_at|completed_at|lease_expires_at|updated_at)"', text),
           "it holds no row timestamp")


class DevTools:
    """A page in the headless browser, over the DevTools protocol: a WebSocket (RFC 6455) client on a
    socket, enough for text frames, which is all the protocol uses."""

    def __init__(self, url, timeout=30):
        match = re.match(r"ws://([^/:]+):(\d+)(/.*)", url)
        if not match:
            raise SystemExit(f"e2e: not a DevTools URL: {url}")
        host, port, path = match.group(1), int(match.group(2)), match.group(3)
        self.sock = socket.create_connection((host, port), timeout=timeout)
        key = base64.b64encode(os.urandom(16)).decode()
        self.sock.sendall(
            f"GET {path} HTTP/1.1\r\nHost: {host}:{port}\r\nUpgrade: websocket\r\n"
            f"Connection: Upgrade\r\nSec-WebSocket-Key: {key}\r\nSec-WebSocket-Version: 13\r\n\r\n"
            .encode()
        )
        head = b""
        while b"\r\n\r\n" not in head:
            chunk = self.sock.recv(4096)
            if not chunk:
                raise SystemExit("e2e: the browser closed the DevTools connection")
            head += chunk
        head, self.buffer = head.split(b"\r\n\r\n", 1)
        if not head.startswith(b"HTTP/1.1 101"):
            raise SystemExit(f"e2e: the browser refused the DevTools connection: {head[:200]!r}")
        self.next_id = 0
        self.events = []

    def _read(self, n):
        while len(self.buffer) < n:
            chunk = self.sock.recv(65536)
            if not chunk:
                raise SystemExit("e2e: the browser closed the DevTools connection")
            self.buffer += chunk
        data, self.buffer = self.buffer[:n], self.buffer[n:]
        return data

    def _frame(self):
        """The next message's text, joining continuation frames."""
        message = b""
        while True:
            first, second = self._read(2)
            length = second & 0x7F
            if length == 126:
                length = struct.unpack(">H", self._read(2))[0]
            elif length == 127:
                length = struct.unpack(">Q", self._read(8))[0]
            payload = self._read(length)
            opcode = first & 0x0F
            if opcode == 8:
                raise SystemExit("e2e: the browser closed the DevTools connection")
            if opcode == 9:
                self._send(10, payload)
                continue
            message += payload
            if first & 0x80:
                return message.decode()

    def _send(self, opcode, payload):
        mask = os.urandom(4)
        header = bytes([0x80 | opcode])
        if len(payload) < 126:
            header += bytes([0x80 | len(payload)])
        elif len(payload) < 1 << 16:
            header += bytes([0x80 | 126]) + struct.pack(">H", len(payload))
        else:
            header += bytes([0x80 | 127]) + struct.pack(">Q", len(payload))
        masked = bytes(b ^ mask[i % 4] for i, b in enumerate(payload))
        self.sock.sendall(header + mask + masked)

    def call(self, method, **params):
        """Calls a method and returns its result, keeping the events that come meanwhile."""
        self.next_id += 1
        self._send(1, json.dumps({"id": self.next_id, "method": method, "params": params}).encode())
        while True:
            message = json.loads(self._frame())
            if message.get("id") == self.next_id:
                if "error" in message:
                    raise SystemExit(f"e2e: DevTools {method} failed: {message['error']}")
                return message.get("result", {})
            if "method" in message:
                self.events.append(message)

    def evaluate(self, expression):
        result = self.call("Runtime.evaluate", expression=expression, returnByValue=True)
        if "exceptionDetails" in result:
            raise SystemExit(f"e2e: the page threw on {expression!r}: {result['exceptionDetails']}")
        return result["result"].get("value")

    def wait(self, what, expression, within):
        return wait_for(what, lambda: self.evaluate(expression), within=within, every=0.2)

    def close(self):
        self.sock.close()


def open_page():
    """A new tab in the browser, as a DevTools connection."""
    port = compose("port", "browser", "9222", capture=True).strip().rsplit(":", 1)[1]
    request = urllib.request.Request(f"http://127.0.0.1:{port}/json/new?about:blank", method="PUT")
    target = wait_for(
        "the browser to answer",
        lambda: _try_json(request),
        within=30,
    )
    # the browser names its own address; it's reached at the published port
    url = re.sub(r"^ws://[^/]+", f"ws://127.0.0.1:{port}", target["webSocketDebuggerUrl"])
    page = DevTools(url)
    for domain in ("Page", "Runtime", "Log"):
        page.call(f"{domain}.enable")
    return page


def _try_json(request):
    try:
        with urllib.request.urlopen(request, timeout=10) as response:
            return json.load(response)
    except OSError:
        return None


def web_request(method, path, body=None, headers=None):
    """One request to the GUI's and the JSON API's port, not following a redirect: its status, headers
    and body."""
    connection = http.client.HTTPConnection("127.0.0.1", int(PORT), timeout=30)
    try:
        connection.request(method, path, body=body, headers=headers or {})
        response = connection.getresponse()
        return response.status, dict(response.getheaders()), response.read().decode()
    finally:
        connection.close()


def sign_in():
    """The analyst's session headers for the JSON API, or None when the login fails."""
    origin = f"http://127.0.0.1:{PORT}"
    form = urllib.parse.urlencode({"username": ANALYST, "password": ANALYST_PASSWORD})
    status, headers, _ = web_request("POST", "/login", form, {
        "Content-Type": "application/x-www-form-urlencoded", "Origin": origin})
    cookie = (headers.get("Set-Cookie") or headers.get("set-cookie") or "").split(";")[0]
    if status != 303 or not cookie:
        return None
    return {"Cookie": cookie, "Origin": origin, "Content-Type": "application/json"}


def started_at(service):
    """When the service's container last started, by Docker's clock."""
    container = compose("ps", "-q", service, capture=True).strip()
    return subprocess.run(
        ["docker", "inspect", "-f", "{{.State.StartedAt}}", container],
        check=True, capture_output=True, text=True,
    ).stdout.strip()


def check_list_edit(email, failures):
    """PLAN.md 5.14's Done check: an entry added through the JSON API applies to the next task with
    nothing restarted, and its audit row names the actor. The entry enables the e2e email's sender for
    detection on the observable_detection list, ace3's observable_detections: the email's sender gets a
    detection and the root alerts. The entry is deleted again, also through the API, before anything
    else runs. (It was the email module's sender whitelist until ace3 removed whitelisting, 8617ba8e.)"""

    def expect(ok, message):
        log(("ok    " if ok else "FAIL  ") + message)
        if not ok:
            failures.append(f"list edit: {message}")

    session = sign_in()
    if session is None:
        expect(False, "the analyst signed in")
        return
    started = {service: started_at(service) for service in ("ace", "parsers")}
    entries = "/api/lists/v1/lists/observable_detection/entries"
    status, _, body = web_request("POST", entries, json.dumps({
        "match": "exact", "value": "alice@example.com", "ignore_case": False,
        "observable_type": "email_address", "note": "the e2e test's sender",
    }), session)
    if status != 201:
        expect(False, f"adding the entry answered {status}: {body}")
        return
    entry = json.loads(body)["id"]
    try:
        root = submit(email)
        log(f"submitted root {root} with its sender enabled for detection")
        seconds = wait_for(f"root {root} to complete", lambda: completed_after(root), within=120)
        log(f"root {root} completed {seconds:.2f}s after it was created")
        flagged = sql(
            f"""SELECT r.details->>'for_detection' FROM analysis.results r
                JOIN analysis.observables o ON o.id = r.observable_id
                WHERE r.root_id = '{root}' AND r.module = 'observable_detection'
                  AND o.type = 'email_address' AND o.value = 'alice@example.com'"""
        )
        expect(flagged == [["true"]], f"the sender was found enabled for detection: {flagged}")
        alerted = sql(f"SELECT alerted_at IS NOT NULL FROM analysis.roots WHERE id = '{root}'")
        expect(alerted == [["t"]], f"its detection made the root an alert: {alerted}")
        audit = sql(
            f"""SELECT actor->>'kind', actor->>'name', action FROM service.audit
                WHERE target_kind = 'list_entry' AND target_id = '{entry}' ORDER BY id"""
        )
        expect(audit == [["user", ANALYST, "add_list_entry"]],
               f"the entry's audit row names the analyst: {audit}")
        now = {service: started_at(service) for service in ("ace", "parsers")}
        expect(now == started, f"nothing restarted: {started} then {now}")
    finally:
        status, _, body = web_request(
            "DELETE", f"{entries}/{entry}", None, session)
        expect(status == 204, f"the entry was deleted through the API ({status} {body})")
        audit = sql(
            f"""SELECT actor->>'name', action FROM service.audit
                WHERE target_kind = 'list_entry' AND target_id = '{entry}' ORDER BY id"""
        )
        expect(audit[-1:] == [[ANALYST, "delete_list_entry"]],
               f"the delete's audit row names the analyst: {audit}")
        left = sql("SELECT count(*) FROM lists.entries")[0][0]
        expect(left == "0", f"the lists are empty again, as ace3's trees were made: {left}")


def check_gui_command(failures):
    """PLAN.md 5.12: a command started with the analyst's session runs on the parser pool, contained,
    on ace's own command line: --help completes with the usage, and a command that needs what a contained
    process can't have is refused."""
    session = sign_in()
    if session is None:
        log("FAIL  the analyst couldn't sign in for a GUI command")
        failures.append("no session for a GUI command")
        return
    ended = {}
    for line in ("--help", "serve"):
        status, _, body = web_request("POST", "/api/cli/v1/commands",
                               json.dumps({"command": line, "timeout_seconds": 60}), session)
        if status != 202:
            log(f"FAIL  starting `ace {line}` answered {status}: {body}")
            failures.append(f"`ace {line}` didn't start")
            return
        run = json.loads(body)["id"]

        def done(run=run):
            status, _, body = web_request("GET", f"/api/cli/v1/commands/{run}", None, session)
            command = json.loads(body) if status == 200 else {}
            return command if command.get("state") not in (None, "queued", "running") else None

        ended[line] = wait_for(f"GUI command `ace {line}` to end", done, within=90)
    help_run, serve_run = ended["--help"], ended["serve"]
    ok = (help_run["state"] == "completed" and help_run["exit_code"] == 0
          and "Usage: ace" in help_run["output"] and "serve" in help_run["output"])
    log(("ok    " if ok else "FAIL  ")
        + f"`ace --help` ran contained on the parser pool: {help_run['state']}, exit "
        + f"{help_run['exit_code']}, {len(help_run['output'])} characters of output")
    if not ok:
        log(json.dumps(help_run, indent=2))
        failures.append("`ace --help` didn't complete from the GUI")
    ok = (serve_run["state"] == "completed" and serve_run["exit_code"] == 2
          and "doesn't run from the GUI" in serve_run["output"])
    log(("ok    " if ok else "FAIL  ") + "`ace serve` was refused as a GUI command: "
        + serve_run["output"].strip())
    if not ok:
        failures.append("`ace serve` wasn't refused as a GUI command")


def make_analyst():
    """The first user, holding every permission, as an operator makes one (PLAN.md 5.4)."""
    result = subprocess.run(
        [*COMPOSE, "exec", "-T", "ace", ACE_COMMAND, "user", "create-first", ANALYST,
         "--password-stdin"],
        env=ENV, cwd=COMPOSE_FILE.parent, input=ANALYST_PASSWORD + "\n", text=True,
        capture_output=True,
    )
    if result.returncode != 0:
        raise SystemExit(f"e2e: `ace user create-first` failed:\n{result.stderr}")


def has_browser():
    """Whether the Compose file has the browser service. ace-rs's does; a site's may not yet, and then the
    browser test is skipped, saying so."""
    services = compose("config", "--services", capture=True).split()
    return "browser" in services


def check_live_alert(email, failures):
    """PLAN.md 5.8: a result that lands appears on an open alert page without a reload."""

    def expect(ok, message):
        log(("ok    " if ok else "FAIL  ") + message)
        if not ok:
            failures.append(f"the browser test: {message}")
        return ok

    page = open_page()
    try:
        page.call("Page.navigate", url=f"{GUI_IN_STACK}/login")
        page.wait("the login page", "document.readyState === 'complete' && "
                  "document.querySelector('form[action=\"/login\"]') !== null", within=30)
        page.evaluate(
            "(() => { const f = document.querySelector('form[action=\"/login\"]');"
            f" f.username.value = {json.dumps(ANALYST)}; f.password.value = {json.dumps(ANALYST_PASSWORD)};"
            " f.submit(); })()"
        )
        page.wait("the login", "location.pathname === '/' && document.readyState === 'complete' && "
                  f"document.getElementById('username')?.textContent === {json.dumps(ANALYST)}",
                  within=30)
        log("ok    the browser logged in to the GUI")

        compose("restart", "responder")
        compose("up", "-d", "--wait", "responder")
        compose("pause", "lookups")
        try:
            root = submit(email)
            log(f"submitted root {root} with the network pool frozen")
            try:
                wait_for(
                    f"root {root} to be an alert with its YARA result",
                    lambda: sql(
                        f"""SELECT 1 FROM analysis.roots r WHERE r.id = '{root}'
                            AND r.alerted_at IS NOT NULL AND EXISTS (
                              SELECT FROM analysis.results x WHERE x.root_id = r.id
                              AND x.module = 'yara_scanner_v3_4')"""
                    ),
                    within=120,
                )
            except SystemExit:
                for row in tasks(root):
                    log("  task " + " | ".join(row))
                raise
            # the page starts at the branches that carry a detection, with the whole tree a link away
            page.events.clear()
            page.call("Page.navigate", url=f"{GUI_IN_STACK}/alerts/{root}")
            page.wait("the alert page", "document.readyState === 'complete' && "
                      "document.getElementById('alert-tree') !== null", within=30)
            whole = page.evaluate(
                "document.querySelector('#alert-tree .tree-scope a')?.getAttribute('href') ?? null"
            )
            pruned = page.evaluate(
                "[...document.querySelectorAll('#alert-tree .result')].map(r => r.dataset.module)"
            )
            expect(whole == "?tree=full#analysis" and "yara_scanner_v3_4" in pruned,
                   f"the alert page starts at its detections' branches, with a link to the whole "
                   f"tree: {whole}, {pruned}")
            # the whole tree, which is where a result on an observable with no detection lands
            page.events.clear()
            page.call("Page.navigate", url=f"{GUI_IN_STACK}/alerts/{root}?tree=full")
            page.wait("the alert page with its whole tree", "document.readyState === 'complete' && "
                      "document.getElementById('alert-tree') !== null", within=30)
            page.evaluate("window.aceRsE2eMarker = 'the page as it was loaded'")
            navigations = len([e for e in page.events if e["method"] == "Page.frameNavigated"])
            before = page.evaluate(
                "[...document.querySelectorAll('#alert-tree .result')].map(r => r.dataset.module)"
            )
            expect("yara_scanner_v3_4" in before and "rdap_analyzer" not in before,
                   f"the open page has the parser pool's results and no RDAP result: {before}")
        finally:
            compose("unpause", "lookups")
        log("let the network pool go; waiting for the RDAP result on the open page")
        try:
            page.wait(
                "the RDAP result to appear on the open page",
                "document.querySelector('#alert-tree [data-module=\"rdap_analyzer\"]') !== null",
                within=120,
            )
            appeared = True
        except SystemExit as error:
            log(str(error))
            appeared = False
        expect(appeared, "the RDAP result appeared on the open page")
        same = page.evaluate("window.aceRsE2eMarker") == "the page as it was loaded"
        later = len([e for e in page.events if e["method"] == "Page.frameNavigated"])
        expect(same and later == navigations, "the page wasn't reloaded or navigated")
        refused = [
            e["params"]["entry"]["text"] for e in page.events
            if e["method"] == "Log.entryAdded"
            and re.search(r"Content.Security.Policy|Refused to", e["params"]["entry"]["text"])
        ]
        expect(not refused, f"the page's policy refused nothing: {refused}")
        check_result_pages(page, expect)
        wait_for(f"root {root} to complete", lambda: completed_after(root), within=300)
        check_graph(page, root, expect)
        check_owner_notice(page, root, expect)
        check_alert_list(page, root, expect)
        check_range_selection(page, expect)
    finally:
        page.close()


def check_result_pages(page, expect):
    """PLAN.md 5.9: a result's summary in the open alert's tree links to its page, which draws it with
    its module's analysis view, and the page's policy refuses nothing there either."""
    # read every link off the alert's page first, since each one leaves it
    modules = ("yara_scanner_v3_4", "rdap_analyzer")
    hrefs = {
        module: page.evaluate(
            f"document.querySelector('#alert-tree [data-module=\"{module}\"] a.summary')"
            "?.getAttribute('href') ?? null"
        )
        for module in modules
    }
    for module, href in hrefs.items():
        if not expect(bool(href), f"the {module} result links to its page: {href}"):
            continue
        page.events.clear()
        page.call("Page.navigate", url=f"{GUI_IN_STACK}{href}")
        page.wait(f"the {module} result's page", "document.readyState === 'complete' && "
                  "document.querySelector('.analysis-view') !== null", within=30)
        own = page.evaluate(
            "!document.querySelector('.result-page').textContent.includes('has no view') && "
            "document.querySelector('.analysis-view table, .analysis-view .panel') !== null"
        )
        expect(own, f"the {module} result's page draws it with its own view")
        refused = [
            e["params"]["entry"]["text"] for e in page.events
            if e["method"] == "Log.entryAdded"
            and re.search(r"Content.Security.Policy|Refused to", e["params"]["entry"]["text"])
        ]
        expect(not refused, f"the {module} result's page: the policy refused nothing: {refused}")


def check_graph(page, root, expect):
    """PLAN.md 5.13: the alert page's Graph link opens its relationship graph, which vis.js draws from the
    JSON API's graph of the alert. The library holds a node for the alert and for each observable, result
    and tag the alert has, each laid out, the email, its attachment, the domain and each module's result
    among them, and the page's policy refuses nothing and nothing throws."""
    page.events.clear()
    page.call("Page.navigate", url=f"{GUI_IN_STACK}/alerts/{root}")
    page.wait("the alert page", "document.readyState === 'complete' && "
              "document.getElementById('alert-tree') !== null", within=30)
    href = page.evaluate(
        "[...document.querySelectorAll('a')].find(a => a.textContent === 'Graph')?.getAttribute('href')"
        " ?? null"
    )
    if not expect(href == f"/alerts/{root}/graph", f"the alert page links to its graph: {href}"):
        return
    page.call("Page.navigate", url=f"{GUI_IN_STACK}{href}")
    try:
        page.wait("vis.js to draw the graph", "document.getElementById('graph')?.dataset.drawn === 'true'",
                  within=60)
        drawn = True
    except SystemExit as error:
        log(str(error))
        drawn = False
    status = page.evaluate("document.getElementById('graph-status')?.textContent ?? null")
    if not expect(drawn, f"vis.js drew the alert's graph: {status}"):
        return
    state = page.evaluate(
        """(() => {
            const graph = document.getElementById('graph');
            const { network, nodes, edges } = graph.aceGraph;
            const positions = network.getPositions();
            const canvas = graph.querySelector('canvas');
            return {
                labels: nodes.get().map(n => n.label),
                laidOut: nodes.getIds().every(id => Number.isFinite(positions[id]?.x)
                                                    && Number.isFinite(positions[id]?.y)),
                edges: edges.length,
                canvas: canvas ? [canvas.width, canvas.height] : null,
            };
        })()"""
    )
    counts = sql(
        f"""SELECT (SELECT count(*) FROM analysis.observables WHERE root_id = '{root}'),
                   (SELECT count(*) FROM analysis.results WHERE root_id = '{root}'),
                   (SELECT count(DISTINCT t) FROM (
                      SELECT unnest(tags) AS t FROM analysis.observables WHERE root_id = '{root}'
                      UNION SELECT unnest(tags) FROM analysis.results WHERE root_id = '{root}') tags)"""
    )[0]
    observables, results, tags = (int(n) for n in counts)
    labels = state["labels"]
    expect(len(labels) == 1 + observables + results + tags,
           f"the graph has a node for the alert and each of its {observables} observables, {results} "
           f"results and {tags} tags: {len(labels)}")
    wanted = ["file: email.rfc822", "DKIM Signing Domain (email_dkim_signing_domain): example.com",
              *MODULES]
    missing = [label for label in wanted if label not in labels]
    if not any(label.startswith("file: ") and label.endswith("invoice.zip") for label in labels):
        missing.append("file: ...invoice.zip")
    expect(not missing, f"the graph has the email, its attachment, the domain and each module's result: "
                        f"missing {missing} of {sorted(labels)}")
    expect(state["laidOut"] and state["edges"] >= len(labels) - 1 and state["canvas"]
           and min(state["canvas"]) > 0,
           f"vis.js laid out every node on its canvas: {state['edges']} edges, canvas {state['canvas']}")
    refused = [
        e["params"]["entry"]["text"] for e in page.events
        if e["method"] == "Log.entryAdded"
        and re.search(r"Content.Security.Policy|Refused to", e["params"]["entry"]["text"])
    ]
    expect(not refused, f"the graph's policy refused nothing: {refused}")
    thrown = [e["params"]["exceptionDetails"].get("text") for e in page.events
              if e["method"] == "Runtime.exceptionThrown"]
    expect(not thrown, f"nothing on the graph's page threw: {thrown}")


def check_owner_notice(page, root, expect):
    """The ownership-changed notice (the owner's decision of 2026-11-15): the browser has the alert's
    page open, a second analyst takes the alert from a session of their own, and the open page says who
    owns it now, pushed by its live stream, with no reload and nothing the page's policy refused."""
    page.events.clear()
    page.call("Page.navigate", url=f"{GUI_IN_STACK}/alerts/{root}")
    page.wait("the alert page", "document.readyState === 'complete' && "
              "document.getElementById('owner-notice') !== null", within=30)
    notice = "document.getElementById('owner-notice')"
    expect(page.evaluate(f"{notice}.hidden && {notice}.textContent === ''"),
           "the open alert page has no ownership notice while nobody else has taken the alert")
    page.evaluate("window.aceRsE2eMarker = 'the page as it was loaded'")
    navigations = len([e for e in page.events if e["method"] == "Page.frameNavigated"])

    # a second analyst, in a session of their own, takes the alert with the alert page's own form
    result = subprocess.run(
        [*COMPOSE, "exec", "-T", "ace", ACE_COMMAND, "user", "create-first", SECOND_ANALYST,
         "--password-stdin", "--force"],
        env=ENV, cwd=COMPOSE_FILE.parent, input=SECOND_ANALYST_PASSWORD + "\n", text=True,
        capture_output=True,
    )
    if result.returncode != 0:
        raise SystemExit(f"e2e: `ace user create-first --force` failed:\n{result.stderr}")
    origin = f"http://127.0.0.1:{PORT}"
    form_headers = {"Content-Type": "application/x-www-form-urlencoded", "Origin": origin}
    status, headers, _ = web_request("POST", "/login", urllib.parse.urlencode(
        {"username": SECOND_ANALYST, "password": SECOND_ANALYST_PASSWORD}), form_headers)
    cookie = (headers.get("Set-Cookie") or headers.get("set-cookie") or "").split(";")[0]
    if status != 303 or not cookie:
        raise SystemExit(f"e2e: the second analyst's login answered {status}")
    status, headers, body = web_request("POST", "/alerts/owner", urllib.parse.urlencode(
        {"alert": root, "owner": "me", "next": f"/alerts/{root}"}), {**form_headers, "Cookie": cookie})
    took = sql(f"""SELECT u.username FROM analysis.roots r JOIN service.users u ON u.id = r.owner_id
                   WHERE r.id = '{root}'""")
    expect(status == 303 and took == [[SECOND_ANALYST]],
           f"the second analyst took the alert through the alert page's form: {status}, {took}")
    log("the second analyst took the alert; waiting for the notice on the open page")
    try:
        page.wait(
            "the ownership notice to appear on the open page",
            f"!{notice}.hidden && {notice}.textContent.includes('Alert Ownership Changed!')",
            within=60,
        )
        appeared = True
    except SystemExit as error:
        log(str(error))
        appeared = False
    text = page.evaluate(f"{notice}.textContent")
    expect(appeared and SECOND_ANALYST in text,
           f"the open page says the alert's ownership changed, and to whom: {text!r}")
    expect(page.evaluate(f"{notice}.getAttribute('role')") == "alert",
           "the notice is an alert to assistive technology")
    same = page.evaluate("window.aceRsE2eMarker") == "the page as it was loaded"
    later = len([e for e in page.events if e["method"] == "Page.frameNavigated"])
    expect(same and later == navigations, "the page wasn't reloaded or navigated for the notice")
    refused = [
        e["params"]["entry"]["text"] for e in page.events
        if e["method"] == "Log.entryAdded"
        and re.search(r"Content.Security.Policy|Refused to", e["params"]["entry"]["text"])
    ]
    expect(not refused, f"the notice: the page's policy refused nothing: {refused}")
    # the second analyst gives the alert back, so the next check's client, which owns nothing, may
    # disposition it: a disposition leaves another analyst's alert alone
    status, _, _ = web_request("POST", "/alerts/owner", urllib.parse.urlencode(
        {"alert": root, "owner": "assign", "assignee": "", "next": f"/alerts/{root}"}),
        {**form_headers, "Cookie": cookie})
    left = sql(f"SELECT owner_id IS NULL FROM analysis.roots WHERE id = '{root}'")
    expect(status == 303 and left == [["t"]],
           f"the second analyst unassigned the alert again: {status}, {left}")


def disposition_elsewhere(root, disposition):
    """Sets an alert's disposition through the JSON API with a key of its own, as another analyst's
    client would, and not through the open page."""
    out = compose(
        "exec", "-T", "ace", ACE_COMMAND, "user", "create-key", "e2e-dispositioner",
        "--grant", "alert:write", capture=True,
    )
    token = next(
        (line.split(": ", 1)[1] for line in out.splitlines()
         if line.startswith("token (shown once): ")),
        None,
    )
    if not token:
        raise SystemExit(f"e2e: `ace user create-key` printed no token:\n{out}")
    request = urllib.request.Request(
        f"http://127.0.0.1:{PORT}/api/alerts/v1/alerts/{root}/disposition",
        data=json.dumps({"disposition": disposition}).encode(),
        method="PUT",
        headers={"Authorization": f"Bearer {token}", "Content-Type": "application/json"},
    )
    with urllib.request.urlopen(request, timeout=30) as response:
        if response.status != 200:
            raise SystemExit(f"e2e: the disposition answered {response.status}")


def check_alert_list(page, root, expect):
    """PLAN.md 5.10: the alert list at / filters the alerts, and its refresh drops an alert that another
    client dispositioned from an open list of open alerts, with no reload, and nothing the page's policy
    refused."""
    row = json.dumps(f"alert-row-{root}")
    rows = "document.querySelectorAll('#alert-list tr[id^=\"alert-row-\"]').length"

    def show(query):
        page.call("Page.navigate", url=f"{GUI_IN_STACK}/{query}")
        page.wait(f"the alert list at /{query}", "document.readyState === 'complete' && "
                  "document.getElementById('alert-list') !== null", within=30)

    page.events.clear()
    show("?f=disposition:OPEN")
    expect(page.evaluate(f"document.getElementById({row}) !== null"),
           "the alert list of open alerts shows the open alert")
    show("?f=description:no-such-alert-in-e2e")
    expect(page.evaluate(rows) == 0, "a filter that matches nothing lists nothing")
    show("?f=disposition:OPEN")
    page.evaluate("window.aceRsE2eMarker = 'the list as it was loaded'")
    navigations = len([e for e in page.events if e["method"] == "Page.frameNavigated"])
    disposition_elsewhere(root, "FALSE_POSITIVE")
    log("dispositioned the alert through the API; waiting for the open list's refresh to drop it")
    try:
        page.wait("the refresh to drop the dispositioned alert",
                  f"document.getElementById({row}) === null", within=75)
        dropped = True
    except SystemExit as error:
        log(str(error))
        dropped = False
    expect(dropped, "the open list's refresh dropped the alert dispositioned elsewhere")
    same = page.evaluate("window.aceRsE2eMarker") == "the list as it was loaded"
    later = len([e for e in page.events if e["method"] == "Page.frameNavigated"])
    expect(same and later == navigations, "the list wasn't reloaded or navigated")
    refused = [
        e["params"]["entry"]["text"] for e in page.events
        if e["method"] == "Log.entryAdded"
        and re.search(r"Content.Security.Policy|Refused to", e["params"]["entry"]["text"])
    ]
    expect(not refused, f"the list's policy refused nothing: {refused}")


def check_root_metrics(roots, failures):
    """The per-root metrics event (ace3 972058d1 and 6a9cd43f, `ace_core::metrics`): the core's log, which
    is where the event is shipped from, has one `METRICS (root)` record for each pass each of these
    roots completed and no more, and the last one's counts are the root's. Its `METRICS (module)`
    records for that pass are one for each module with a run in it, with the module's run time and
    runs as the tasks' rows have them, adding up to the root event's `total_analysis_time_seconds`."""

    def expect(ok, message):
        log(("ok    " if ok else "FAIL  ") + message)
        if not ok:
            failures.append(f"the metrics event: {message}")
        return ok

    prefix, module_prefix = "METRICS (root): ", "METRICS (module): "
    decoder = json.JSONDecoder()
    events, module_events = [], []
    for line in compose("logs", "--no-color", "ace", capture=True).splitlines():
        for mark, found in ((prefix, events), (module_prefix, module_events)):
            at = line.find(mark)
            if at >= 0:
                found.append(decoder.raw_decode(line[at + len(mark):])[0])
    for root in roots:
        mine = [event for event in events if event["root_uuid"] == root]
        row = sql(
            f"""SELECT (SELECT count(*) FROM queue.root_completions WHERE root_id = r.id),
                       (SELECT count(*) FROM analysis.observables WHERE root_id = r.id),
                       (SELECT count(*) FROM queue.tasks
                        WHERE root_id = r.id AND module <> 'core_hooks'),
                       (SELECT count(*) FROM queue.tasks
                        WHERE root_id = r.id AND module <> 'core_hooks' AND state = 'failed'),
                       r.alerted_at IS NOT NULL, r.queue
                FROM analysis.roots r WHERE r.id = '{root}'"""
        )[0]
        passes, observables, tasks, failed = (int(n) for n in row[:4])
        if not expect(passes >= 1 and [event["pass"] for event in mine] == list(range(1, passes + 1)),
                      f"the core logged one event for each of root {root}'s {passes} passes: "
                      f"{[event['pass'] for event in mine]}"):
            continue
        last = mine[-1]
        expect(last["event_type"] == "root"
               and last["observable_count"] == observables
               and sum(last["observable_type_counts"].values()) == observables
               and last["task_count"] == tasks and last["failed_task_count"] == failed
               and last["is_alert"] == (row[4] == "t") and last["queue"] == row[5]
               and last["outcome"] == "completed" and last["pass_open_seconds"] > 0
               and last["total_analysis_time_seconds"] > 0,
               f"its last event has the root's counts ({observables} observables, {tasks} tasks, "
               f"{failed} failed): {json.dumps(last)}")
        runs = {
            module: (float(seconds), int(count))
            for module, seconds, count in sql(
                f"""SELECT module, sum(run_seconds), sum(runs) FROM queue.tasks
                    WHERE root_id = '{root}' AND run_pass = {last["pass"]} AND runs > 0
                    GROUP BY module"""
            )
        }
        modules = [event for event in module_events
                   if event["root_uuid"] == root and event["pass"] == last["pass"]]
        logged = {event["module"]: (event["analysis_time_seconds"], event["exec_count"])
                  for event in modules}
        expect(len(modules) == len(logged) and logged.keys() == runs.keys()
               and all(abs(logged[m][0] - runs[m][0]) < 1e-6 and logged[m][1] == runs[m][1]
                       for m in runs)
               and all(event["timestamp"] == last["timestamp"] for event in modules)
               and abs(sum(seconds for seconds, _ in logged.values())
                       - last["total_analysis_time_seconds"]) < 1e-6
               and abs(sum(event["percentage"] for event in modules) - 100) < 1e-6,
               f"its pass's module events are one for each of the {len(runs)} modules that ran, "
               f"with their run times, adding up to the root's: {json.dumps(modules)}")


def check_range_selection(page, expect):
    """Ticking a range of alerts on the list (ace3 5fb36276, static/select.js), with a real pointer and
    keyboard: the browser's own mouse and key events, sent over the DevTools protocol, on a list of
    eight alerts made here. A shift+click ticks the rows from the last one clicked, and unticks them
    when it unticks its own box; a drag over the boxes ticks the rows it passes and puts back the ones
    it leaves, and a release back on its first box leaves that box ticked. Then the list refreshes
    underneath, twice: the ticked rows stay ticked and a row the refresh brought in isn't, the anchor
    outlives the refresh, and once the refresh has dropped the anchor's row a shift+click ticks its
    own box alone. The box at the head of the column leaves the anchor where it was. Shift+Space ticks
    a range from the keyboard. Last, the bulk form posts exactly the ticked rows, which Set
    Disposition then dispositions. Nothing the page's policy refused, and nothing thrown."""
    made = [str(uuid.uuid4()) for _ in range(9)]

    def add(n, minutes_ago):
        sql(f"""INSERT INTO analysis.roots
                    (id, analysis_mode, description, event_time_source, alerted_at)
                VALUES ('{made[n]}', 'correlation', 'e2e-range-{n}', 'unset',
                        now() - interval '{minutes_ago} minutes')""")

    def remove(n):
        sql(f"DELETE FROM analysis.roots WHERE id = '{made[n]}'")

    boxes = "[...document.querySelectorAll('#alert-list input[name=\"alert\"]')]"

    def names(ids):
        return [made.index(i) if i in made else i for i in ids]

    def rows():
        return names(page.evaluate(f"{boxes}.map(b => b.value)"))

    def ticked():
        return names(page.evaluate(f"{boxes}.filter(b => b.checked).map(b => b.value)"))

    def is_ticked(wanted, what):
        try:
            wait_for(what, lambda: ticked() == wanted, within=5, every=0.1)
        except SystemExit:
            pass
        found = ticked()
        return expect(found == wanted, f"{what}: rows {found} are ticked")

    def centre(selector):
        point = page.evaluate(
            f"(() => {{ const r = document.querySelector({json.dumps(selector)})"
            ".getBoundingClientRect(); return [r.left + r.width / 2, r.top + r.height / 2]; })()"
        )
        return point[0], point[1]

    def box(n):
        return f'#alert-list input[name="alert"][value="{made[n]}"]'

    def mouse(kind, selector, shift=False):
        x, y = centre(selector)
        held = kind in ("mousePressed", "mouseDragged")
        page.call(
            "Input.dispatchMouseEvent",
            type="mouseMoved" if kind == "mouseDragged" else kind,
            x=x, y=y,
            button="none" if kind == "mouseMoved" else "left",
            buttons=1 if held else 0,
            clickCount=0 if kind in ("mouseMoved", "mouseDragged") else 1,
            modifiers=8 if shift else 0,
        )

    def click(selector, shift=False):
        mouse("mouseMoved", selector, shift)
        mouse("mousePressed", selector, shift)
        mouse("mouseReleased", selector, shift)

    def space(shift=False):
        for kind in ("keyDown", "keyUp"):
            page.call(
                "Input.dispatchKeyEvent", type=kind, key=" ", code="Space",
                windowsVirtualKeyCode=32, nativeVirtualKeyCode=32,
                modifiers=8 if shift else 0, **({"text": " "} if kind == "keyDown" else {}),
            )

    def refreshed(wanted, what):
        try:
            wait_for(what, lambda: rows() == wanted, within=75, every=0.5)
        except SystemExit as error:
            log(str(error))
        return expect(rows() == wanted, f"{what}: the list has rows {rows()}")

    try:
        # alert n is n + 1 minutes old, so the list, newest first, has them in order
        for n in range(8):
            add(n, n + 1)
        page.events.clear()
        # tall enough that every row is on the screen, so a drag never scrolls the page under it
        page.call("Emulation.setDeviceMetricsOverride", width=1280, height=1600,
                  deviceScaleFactor=1, mobile=False)
        page.call("Page.navigate", url=f"{GUI_IN_STACK}/?f=description:e2e-range-")
        page.wait("the alert list of the range's alerts", "document.readyState === 'complete' && "
                  "document.getElementById('alert-list') !== null", within=30)
        page.evaluate("window.aceRsE2eMarker = 'the list as it was loaded'")
        navigations = len([e for e in page.events if e["method"] == "Page.frameNavigated"])
        loaded = page.evaluate(
            "[...document.querySelectorAll('script[src]')].map(s => s.getAttribute('src'))"
        )
        expect(len(loaded) == 2 and re.fullmatch(r"/static/select\.[0-9a-f]{16}\.js", loaded[1]),
               f"the list loads Datastar and its own script, from this origin: {loaded}")
        if not expect(rows() == list(range(8)) and ticked() == [],
                      f"the list has the eight alerts, newest first, none ticked: {rows()}"):
            return

        click(box(1))
        is_ticked([1], "a click ticks its row")
        focused = page.evaluate("document.activeElement?.value ?? null")
        expect(focused == made[1], "the clicked box has the focus, for the keyboard to carry on from")
        click(box(4), shift=True)
        is_ticked([1, 2, 3, 4], "a shift+click ticks every row from the last one clicked")
        posted = names(page.evaluate("new FormData(document.getElementById('bulk')).getAll('alert')"))
        expect(posted == [1, 2, 3, 4], f"the bulk form would post the ticked rows: {posted}")
        click(box(2), shift=True)
        is_ticked([1], "a shift+click that unticks its box unticks the range back to the last click")

        # a drag: press on row 5, over rows 6 and 7, back to 6, and let go there
        mouse("mouseMoved", box(5))
        mouse("mousePressed", box(5))
        mouse("mouseDragged", box(6))
        mouse("mouseDragged", box(7))
        is_ticked([1, 5, 6, 7], "a drag ticks the rows it passes over")
        mouse("mouseDragged", box(6))
        is_ticked([1, 5, 6], "and puts back the row it leaves again")
        mouse("mouseReleased", box(6))
        is_ticked([1, 5, 6], "letting go keeps them")
        # a drag that comes back to its first box and lets go there: the click that follows the
        # release must not untick it
        mouse("mouseMoved", box(0))
        mouse("mousePressed", box(0))
        mouse("mouseDragged", box(1))
        mouse("mouseDragged", box(0))
        mouse("mouseReleased", box(0))
        is_ticked([0, 1, 5, 6], "a drag let go on its first box leaves that box ticked")
        selected = page.evaluate("String(window.getSelection())")
        expect(selected == "", f"neither selected the rows' text: {selected!r}")

        # the list refreshes underneath: a new alert arrives at the top and an unticked one goes
        add(8, 0)
        remove(3)
        log("changed the list underneath; waiting for its refresh")
        if not refreshed([8, 0, 1, 2, 4, 5, 6, 7], "the refresh brought the new alert and dropped one"):
            return
        is_ticked([0, 1, 5, 6], "the refresh kept the ticked rows and ticked nothing else")
        click(box(2), shift=True)
        is_ticked([0, 1, 2, 5, 6], "the anchor, the row the drag ended on, outlived the refresh")
        # the anchor is row 2 now; the next refresh drops it
        remove(2)
        log("removed the anchor's alert; waiting for the list's refresh")
        if not refreshed([8, 0, 1, 4, 5, 6, 7], "the refresh dropped the anchor's row"):
            return
        click(box(7), shift=True)
        is_ticked([0, 1, 5, 6, 7], "with its anchor gone, a shift+click ticks its own row alone")

        click("#tick-all")
        is_ticked([8, 0, 1, 4, 5, 6, 7], "the box at the head of the column ticks every row")
        click("#tick-all")
        is_ticked([], "and unticks them")
        click(box(4), shift=True)
        is_ticked([4, 5, 6, 7], "it left the anchor where it was, on the last row")

        # the keyboard: Space ticks the focused box, and Shift+Space ticks the range from it
        page.evaluate(f"document.querySelector({json.dumps(box(8))}).focus()")
        space()
        is_ticked([8, 4, 5, 6, 7], "Space ticks the focused row")
        page.evaluate(f"document.querySelector({json.dumps(box(1))}).focus()")
        space(shift=True)
        is_ticked([8, 0, 1, 4, 5, 6, 7], "Shift+Space ticks the range from the last row ticked")
        click(box(8))
        is_ticked([0, 1, 4, 5, 6, 7], "a click unticks one row of it")

        same = page.evaluate("window.aceRsE2eMarker") == "the list as it was loaded"
        later = len([e for e in page.events if e["method"] == "Page.frameNavigated"])
        expect(same and later == navigations, "the list wasn't reloaded or navigated through all of it")
        refused = [
            e["params"]["entry"]["text"] for e in page.events
            if e["method"] == "Log.entryAdded"
            and re.search(r"Content.Security.Policy|Refused to", e["params"]["entry"]["text"])
        ]
        expect(not refused, f"the list's policy refused nothing: {refused}")
        thrown = [e["params"]["exceptionDetails"].get("text") for e in page.events
                  if e["method"] == "Runtime.exceptionThrown"]
        expect(not thrown, f"nothing on the list threw: {thrown}")

        # the bulk action reads the ticked boxes: Set Disposition dispositions those six alone
        page.evaluate("document.getElementById('bulk-disposition').value = 'FALSE_POSITIVE'")
        click("#bulk button.primary")
        try:
            page.wait("the bulk disposition's answer", "document.readyState === 'complete' && "
                      "location.pathname === '/alerts/disposition'", within=30)
        except SystemExit as error:
            log(str(error))
        dispositioned = sorted(
            int(row[0].rsplit("-", 1)[1]) for row in sql(
                "SELECT description FROM analysis.roots "
                "WHERE description LIKE 'e2e-range-%' AND disposition = 'FALSE_POSITIVE'")
        )
        expect(dispositioned == [0, 1, 4, 5, 6, 7],
               f"Set Disposition dispositioned the ticked alerts and no other: {dispositioned}")
    finally:
        page.call("Emulation.clearDeviceMetricsOverride")
        sql("DELETE FROM analysis.roots WHERE description LIKE 'e2e-range-%'")


def check_search(first, second, failures):
    """PLAN.md 7.11: the indexer indexed both alerts when their passes completed, embedding with the
    model the ace image carries into the pgvector the Postgres image carries, and a search through the
    JSON API finds an alert by its own words, by its id, and as the other's near duplicate."""

    def expect(ok, message):
        log(("ok    " if ok else "FAIL  ") + message)
        if not ok:
            failures.append(f"search: {message}")
        return ok

    for root in (first, second):
        indexed = wait_for(
            f"the search indexer to index {root}",
            lambda root=root: sql(
                f"SELECT documents, chunks, model FROM search.indexed WHERE root_id = '{root}'"),
            within=180,
        )[0]
        expect(int(indexed[0]) >= 2 and int(indexed[1]) >= 2 and indexed[2] == "all-MiniLM-L6-v2",
               f"the indexer indexed {root}: {indexed[0]} documents, {indexed[1]} chunks, with {indexed[2]}")
    wait_for("the indexer to have nothing due",
             lambda: sql("SELECT count(*) FROM search.due")[0][0] == "0", within=180)
    stored = sql(f"""SELECT count(*), min(vector_dims(embedding)), count(DISTINCT kind)
                     FROM search.chunks WHERE root_id = '{first}'""")[0]
    expect(int(stored[0]) >= 2 and stored[1] == "384" and int(stored[2]) >= 2,
           f"its chunks are in Postgres, each with an embedding of 384: {stored}")
    out = compose(
        "exec", "-T", "ace", ACE_COMMAND, "user", "create-key", "e2e-searcher",
        "--grant", "alert:read", capture=True,
    )
    token = next(
        (line.split(": ", 1)[1] for line in out.splitlines()
         if line.startswith("token (shown once): ")),
        None,
    )
    if not token:
        raise SystemExit(f"e2e: `ace user create-key` printed no token:\n{out}")

    def search(route, body):
        request = urllib.request.Request(
            f"http://127.0.0.1:{PORT}/api/search/v1/{route}",
            data=json.dumps(body).encode(),
            method="POST",
            headers={"Authorization": f"Bearer {token}", "Content-Type": "application/json"},
        )
        with urllib.request.urlopen(request, timeout=60) as response:
            return json.load(response)

    # the alert's own title, as plain words: a colon or a quote would make a field term of one
    title = sql(f"SELECT description FROM analysis.roots WHERE id = '{first}'")[0][0]
    words = " ".join(title.replace(":", " ").replace('"', " ").split())
    found = search("alerts", {"query": words, "limit": 10})
    ids = [result["alert"]["id"] for result in found["results"]]
    tiers = {result["alert"]["id"]: result["tier"] for result in found["results"]}
    expect(first in ids and second in ids and not found["errors"] and not found["warnings"]
           and "semantic" in found["lanes_used"] and tiers.get(first) in ("strong", "good"),
           f"a search for the alert's title {words!r} finds both alerts by their text: "
           f"{[(i, tiers[i]) for i in ids]}, lanes {found['lanes_used']}, in {found['timings_ms']} ms")
    hits = next((result["hits"] for result in found["results"] if result["alert"]["id"] == first), [])
    expect(bool(hits) and all(hit["lane"] == "semantic" and hit["text"] for hit in hits),
           f"with the text that matched: {[hit['kind'] for hit in hits]}")
    exact = search("alerts", {"query": f"uuid:{first}"})
    expect([result["alert"]["id"] for result in exact["results"]] == [first]
           and exact["results"][0]["tier"] == "exact" and exact["lanes_used"] == ["lexical"],
           "a search for its id finds it alone, as an exact match")
    nothing = search("alerts", {"query": "xyzzy plugh"})
    expect(nothing["total"] == 0, f"a query that resembles nothing finds nothing: {nothing['total']}")
    similar = search("similar", {"alert_uuid": first, "limit": 5})
    like = [result["alert"]["id"] for result in similar["results"]]
    expect(second in like and first not in like,
           f"the same email's other alert is among those like it, and it isn't among its own: {like}")


def check_ai(first, failures):
    """PLAN.md 7.15: the AI investigation API, on in this stack with ace3's testing backend, served by
    `ace serve-ai` in the `ai` service on a port of its own. A key scoped to it reaches its routes
    there and nothing else anywhere, each call is recorded, and the process holds none of the core's
    secrets and refuses to start when handed one."""

    def expect(ok, message):
        log(("ok    " if ok else "FAIL  ") + message)
        if not ok:
            failures.append(f"ai: {message}")
        return ok

    out = compose(
        "exec", "-T", "ace", ACE_COMMAND, "user", "create-key", "e2e-agent",
        "--grant", "ai:fake", "--grant", "ai:alert", "--grant", "ai:search",
        "--grant", "ai:backends", capture=True,
    )
    token = next(
        (line.split(": ", 1)[1] for line in out.splitlines()
         if line.startswith("token (shown once): ")),
        None,
    )
    if not token:
        raise SystemExit(f"e2e: `ace user create-key` printed no token:\n{out}")

    ai_port = compose("port", "ai", "8001", capture=True).strip().rsplit(":", 1)[1]

    def call(method, path, body=None, port=None):
        """The status and the JSON body, from the AI listener, or the main API's when `port` is its."""
        request = urllib.request.Request(
            f"http://127.0.0.1:{port or ai_port}{path}",
            data=None if body is None else json.dumps(body).encode(),
            method=method,
            headers={"Authorization": f"Bearer {token}", "Content-Type": "application/json"},
        )
        try:
            with urllib.request.urlopen(request, timeout=60) as response:
                return response.status, json.load(response)
        except urllib.error.HTTPError as error:
            text = error.read()
            return error.code, (json.loads(text) if text else {})

    # the process: what it holds, and that it checked
    held = compose("exec", "-T", "ai", "env", capture=True).splitlines()
    names = sorted(line.split("=", 1)[0] for line in held if line.startswith("ACE_RS_"))
    # an AWS credential in the environment is one the bucket's credential chain would take
    aws = sorted(line.split("=", 1)[0] for line in held
                 if line.startswith(("AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=", "AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=", "AWS_SESSION_TOKEN=",
                                     "AWS_WEB_IDENTITY_TOKEN_FILE=", "AWS_CONTAINER_")))
    forbidden = aws + [name for name in names
                       if name in ("ACE_RS_ENCRYPTION_KEY", "ACE_RS_ADMIN_TOKEN", "ACE_RS_POOL_TOKEN", "ACE_RS_API_KEY",
                                   "ACE_RS_BUCKET_ACCESS_KEY", "ACE_RS_BUCKET_SECRET_KEY")
                       or name.startswith("ACE_RS_POOL_TOKEN_")]
    expect(not forbidden and "ACE_RS_DATABASE_URL" in names and "ACE_RS_OVERLAY" in names,
           f"the ai service's environment holds the database and its overlay, and no key, token or "
           f"bucket credential: {names + aws}")
    logs = compose("logs", "ai", capture=True)
    expect("AI API custody checks passed" in logs and "the AI investigation API is on" in logs,
           "the ai service checked what it holds when it started, and turned the API on")
    core_url, _ = database_login("ace")
    _, ai_login = database_login("ai")
    login = sql("SELECT rolsuper OR rolcreaterole OR rolcreatedb OR rolbypassrls, "
                "pg_has_role(rolname, 'ace_rs_ai', 'MEMBER') FROM pg_roles WHERE rolname = '"
                + ai_login.replace("'", "''") + "'")
    expect(login == [["f", "t"]],
           f"its database login, {ai_login}, is a plain member of ace_rs_ai: {login}")
    # handed the email archive's key, or the core's database login, it doesn't start
    for what, args, named in [
        ("the email archive's key", ["-e", "ACE_RS_ENCRYPTION_KEY=" + "00" * 32], "ACE_RS_ENCRYPTION_KEY"),
        ("a pool's token", ["-e", "ACE_RS_POOL_TOKEN_PARSERS=ace-rs-dev-parsers-token"], "ACE_RS_POOL_TOKEN_PARSERS"),
        ("the core's database login", ["-e", f"ACE_RS_DATABASE_URL={core_url}"], "superuser"),
    ]:
        refused = subprocess.run(
            [*COMPOSE, "run", "--rm", "--no-deps", "-T", *args, "ai"],
            env=ENV, cwd=COMPOSE_FILE.parent, text=True, capture_output=True, timeout=120,
        )
        output = refused.stdout + refused.stderr
        expect(refused.returncode != 0 and "AI API custody checks failed, refusing to start" in output
               and named in output and "00" * 32 not in output and "ace-rs-dev-parsers-token" not in output,
               f"handed {what}, `ace serve-ai` refuses to start and names it, not its value: "
               f"exit {refused.returncode}")

    # the routes are the ai service's alone
    status, _ = call("GET", "/api/ai/v1/backends", port=PORT)
    expect(status == 404, f"the main API has no AI route, even for the AI key: {status}")
    status, _ = call("GET", f"/api/alerts/v1/alerts/{first}")
    expect(status == 404, f"and the AI listener has none of the main API's: {status}")
    with urllib.request.urlopen(f"http://127.0.0.1:{ai_port}/api/openapi.json", timeout=30) as response:
        paths = sorted(json.load(response)["paths"])
    expect(len(paths) == 9 and all(p.startswith("/api/ai/v1/") or p == "/api/health/v1/ping" for p in paths),
           f"the AI listener's document lists its eight routes and the ping: {len(paths)} paths")
    with urllib.request.urlopen(f"http://127.0.0.1:{PORT}/api/openapi.json", timeout=30) as response:
        main_paths = list(json.load(response)["paths"])
    expect(not any(p.startswith("/api/ai/") for p in main_paths),
           "and the main API's document lists none of them")

    status, listed = call("GET", "/api/ai/v1/backends")
    backends = {b["name"]: b for b in listed.get("backends", [])}
    expect(status == 200 and list(backends) == ["fake"] and backends["fake"]["authorized"]
           and backends["fake"]["describe"]["query_language"] == "fake",
           f"the key lists the one backend the overlay enables, and reaches it: {status} {list(backends)}")
    status, answer = call("POST", "/api/ai/v1/query/fake", {
        "query": "search e2e", "start_time": "2026-01-01T00:00:00Z", "end_time": "2026-01-01T01:00:00Z",
    })
    expect(status == 200 and answer.get("backend") == "fake" and answer.get("row_count") == 2
           and answer.get("truncated") is False and answer.get("meta") == {"fake": True},
           f"a query answers the backend's canned rows: {status} {answer.get('row_count')} rows")
    status, refused = call("POST", "/api/ai/v1/query/fake", {"query": "search e2e"})
    expect(status == 400 and "requires start_time and end_time" in refused.get("error", ""),
           f"a query with no window is refused: {status} {refused.get('error')}")
    status, alert = call("GET", f"/api/ai/v1/alerts/{first}")
    expect(status == 200 and alert.get("alert", {}).get("id") == first,
           f"the key reads the first alert: {status}")
    status, found = call("POST", "/api/ai/v1/search/alerts", {"query": f"uuid:{first}"})
    expect(status == 200 and [r["alert"]["id"] for r in found.get("results", [])] == [first],
           f"and finds it by its id: {status}")
    status, refused = call("GET", "/api/ai/v1/export/alerts")
    expect(status == 403 and refused.get("error") == "this needs ai:export",
           f"the export needs a permission the key doesn't hold: {status} {refused.get('error')}")
    # a search by meaning reads the index with the embedding model, in the ai service, under its role
    status, found = call("POST", "/api/ai/v1/search/alerts", {"query": "an email with an attachment"})
    expect(status == 200 and "semantic" in found.get("lanes_used", []) and not found.get("errors")
           and not found.get("warnings"),
           f"a search by meaning runs in the ai service: {status}, lanes {found.get('lanes_used')}, "
           f"{found.get('errors')} {found.get('warnings')}")
    status, refused = call("GET", f"/api/alerts/v1/alerts/{first}", port=PORT)
    expect(status == 403 and refused.get("error") == "this needs alert:read",
           f"the main API refuses the key: {status} {refused.get('error')}")

    events = [row[0] for row in sql(
        "SELECT details->>'event' FROM service.audit WHERE action = 'ai_record' "
        "AND actor->>'name' = 'e2e-agent' ORDER BY id")]
    expect(events == ["query", "query_rejected", "alert_read", "search", "search"],
           f"each call that reached the service has its audit row, and the refusals none: {events}")
    recorded = sql(
        "SELECT details->>'query', details->>'row_count', details ? 'rows' FROM service.audit "
        "WHERE action = 'ai_record' AND details->>'event' = 'query'")[0]
    expect(recorded == ["search e2e", "2", "f"],
           f"the query's row holds what was asked and how much came back, not the rows: {recorded}")
    counted = sql("SELECT count FROM ai.windows WHERE bucket = 'fake' AND kind = 'minute'")
    expect(sum(int(row[0]) for row in counted) == 1 and
           sql("SELECT count(*) FROM ai.inflight")[0][0] == "0",
           f"the limiter counted the one query that ran, in Postgres, and holds no slot: {counted}")


def check_library_diff(failures):
    """That the library diff (PLAN.md 4.8) has teeth. Its full run over the sample set is a separate
    invocation, tools/library-diff/run --all, since it takes as long as the comparison."""
    started = time.monotonic()
    code = subprocess.run([ROOT / "tools" / "library-diff" / "self-test"]).returncode
    log(("ok    " if code == 0 else "FAIL  ") + "the library diff's self-test "
        f"({time.monotonic() - started:.1f}s)")
    if code != 0:
        failures.append("the library diff's self-test failed; see above")


def check_module_inventory(failures):
    """That docs/modules.md names every analysis module section in ace3's config and no other
    (PLAN.md 7.1), with what serves each read of ACE's data (7.2) and a decision for each program
    a module starts (7.3)."""
    command = [ROOT / "tools" / "ace3" / "modules" / "check"]
    if os.environ.get("CI"):
        command.append("--allow-absent")
    if subprocess.run(command).returncode != 0:
        failures.append("the module inventory (docs/modules.md) doesn't match ace3's config; "
                        "see above")


def check_ports_compared(failures):
    """A port that replaces a Python library must have been compared with something."""
    compared = json.loads((WORK / "compare" / "report.json").read_text())["compared_by_module"]
    for module in LIBRARY_PORTS:
        counts = compared.get(module, {})
        log(f"{module}: {counts}")
        if not counts.get("ace3_results") or not counts.get("ace_rs_results"):
            failures.append(f"{module} was compared with nothing: {counts}")


def give_ace_rs_the_trees_world():
    """What make-trees gave ace3's tagging and detection modules (PLAN.md 7.6), given to ace-rs: the
    observables enabled for detection, through the detection API with a key of their own, the tags
    analysts mapped to observables, with SQL, since ace3 has no API for them either, and the site
    tags, which the overlay holds. Returns why it couldn't, or None."""
    sql("DELETE FROM lists.entries WHERE list = 'observable_detection'; "
        "TRUNCATE analysis.observable_tags")
    # ace3's export names each rule's strings by its detection's id, which make-trees made its place in
    # the file from 1 (PLAN.md 7.16), so ace-rs's entries take the same ids
    left = sql("SELECT count(*) FROM lists.entries")[0][0]
    if left != "0":
        return f"lists.entries holds {left} entries, so the detections can't take the ids ace3's trees have"
    sql("ALTER TABLE lists.entries ALTER COLUMN id RESTART WITH 1")
    out = compose(
        "exec", "-T", "ace", ACE_COMMAND, "user", "create-key", f"e2e-detections-{uuid.uuid4().hex[:8]}",
        "--grant", "detection:write", capture=True,
    )
    token = next((line.split(": ", 1)[1] for line in out.splitlines()
                  if line.startswith("token (shown once): ")), None)
    if not token:
        return f"`ace user create-key` printed no token:\n{out}"
    detections = json.loads((TREES / "detections.json").read_text())["detections"]
    for expected, detection in enumerate(detections, start=1):
        status, _, body = web_request(
            "POST", "/api/observables/v1/detections",
            json.dumps({"type": detection["type"], "value": detection["value"], "expires_on": None,
                        "detection_context": "tools/ace3/trees/detections.json"}),
            {"Authorization": f"Bearer {token}", "Content-Type": "application/json"},
        )
        if status != 201:
            return f"adding the detection {detection} answered {status}: {body}"
        if json.loads(body)["id"] != expected:
            return f"the detection {detection} got the id {json.loads(body)['id']}, not {expected}"
    # the detections are rules of the ruleset too: the core builds them in, and the parser pool
    # switches to that ruleset, before a sample is scanned
    exported = (
        "SELECT key FROM yara.rulesets WHERE id = (SELECT max(id) FROM yara.rulesets) AND "
        "(SELECT sum((t->>'detections')::int) FROM jsonb_array_elements(detection_export->'types') t) = "
        f"{len(detections)}"
    )
    key = wait_for("the core to build the detections into the ruleset", lambda: sql(exported), within=120)[0][0]

    def loaded():
        # the pool's last switch is to that ruleset: an earlier comparison on this stack loaded it too
        switches = [line for line in compose("logs", "parsers", capture=True).splitlines()
                    if "switched to a new ruleset" in line]
        # the line names the ruleset it switched to, then the one it left
        return bool(switches) and key in switches[-1].split("previous")[0]

    wait_for("the parser pool to load the ruleset with the detections", loaded, within=120)
    for mapping in json.loads((TREES / "observable_tags.json").read_text())["tags"]:
        quoted = [mapping[k].replace("'", "''") for k in ("type", "value", "tag")]
        sql("INSERT INTO analysis.observable_tags (type, value, tag) VALUES ('"
            + "', '".join(quoted) + "')")
    overlay = (SITE / "overlay.yaml").read_text()
    missing = [line for line in (TREES / "site_tags.csv").read_text().splitlines()
               if line and f"        {line}\n" not in overlay]
    if missing:
        return f"tests/e2e/site/overlay.yaml's site_tagger csv doesn't have {missing}"
    return None


# The two-run check's samples (PLAN.md decision 26): ones that reach each module the stack runs that opts
# into the analysis cache, after the comparison, so the world is the trees' (the newly registered
# domains, the detections, the tags). qrcode: a PDF whose QR code holds a URL, whose result adds a file
# named after it; a broken PDF, whose clean scan is kept as ace3's are; and the images inside an Office
# document, an encrypted email's zipped attachment, an executable's resources and an HTML page's data
# URLs. pdf_link_text: a PDF with links. rdap_analyzer: the domains in those emails and the QR code's
# URL, which the responder answers. nrd_analyzer: an email whose domains tools/ace3/trees/nrd.json lists.
# site_tagger: a capture whose host a site tag row names, with the cache_ttl this check gives it, since
# ace3 doesn't keep its results by default. ocr runs on no sample: nothing in them gets its directive.
CACHE_SAMPLES = [
    "ace3/pdf/sample_pdf_with_qr_code.pdf",
    "ace-rs/pdf/broken_no_root.pdf",
    "ace3/office/mortgage_payment-0873821-0565.docm",
    "ace-rs/email/encrypted_in_zip.email.rfc822",
    "ace3/executables/cmd-upx.exe",
    "ace-rs/web/data_urls.html",
    "ace-rs/pdf/uri_array.pdf",
    "ace3/email/encrypted_msoffice.email.rfc822",
    "ace3/pcap/http_tls.pcapng",
]
CACHED_MODULES = ["qrcode", "pdf_link_text", "rdap_analyzer", "nrd_analyzer", "site_tagger"]


def use_site(site):
    """Starts the core again on the site directory `site`, and waits for it."""
    ENV[PREFIX + "SITE"] = str(site)
    compose("up", "-d", "--wait", "--no-deps", "--force-recreate", "ace")


def run_samples(paths):
    """Submits each sample as `ace compare` does, waits for each root to complete, and returns the
    roots with their normal forms."""
    manifest = {s["path"]: s for s in json.loads((ROOT / "samples" / "manifest.json").read_text())["samples"]}
    roots = []
    for path in paths:
        sample = manifest[path]
        root = submit_file((ROOT / "samples" / path).read_bytes(), sample["alert_path"], "cli",
                           sample["meta_tags"])
        roots.append((path, root))
    done = []
    for path, root in roots:
        wait_for(f"{path}'s root to complete", lambda root=root: completed_after(root), within=600)
        done.append((path, root, normal_form(root)))
    return done


def cacheable_work(roots):
    """For each sample, what each cacheable module did on each observable, a file by its paths: (whether
    its result has an error, whether it came from the cache, the observable's value) for a result, and
    (None, None, value) for a task that ran in a pool and left none; a task a kept result ended at its
    lease isn't one. A file is named by its paths because some files' bytes, and so their sha256, change
    every run (Ghostscript's rewrite of a PDF), which makes them other inputs with other keys."""
    names = ", ".join(f"'{m}'" for m in CACHED_MODULES)
    label = """CASE WHEN o.type = 'file' THEN 'file@' || (SELECT string_agg(f.path, '|' ORDER BY f.path COLLATE "C")
                                                      FROM analysis.files f
                                                      WHERE f.root_id = o.root_id AND f.observable_id = o.id)
                    ELSE o.type || ':' || o.value END"""
    work = {}
    for path, root, _ in roots:
        for m, o, value, e, c in sql(f"""SELECT r.module, {label}, o.value, r.error IS NOT NULL,
                                               r.cached_at IS NOT NULL
                                        FROM analysis.results r
                                        JOIN analysis.observables o ON o.root_id = r.root_id AND o.id = r.observable_id
                                        WHERE r.root_id = '{root}' AND r.module IN ({names})"""):
            work[(path, m, o)] = (e == "t", c == "t", value)
        for m, o, value in sql(f"""SELECT t.module, {label}, o.value FROM queue.tasks t
                                  JOIN analysis.observables o ON o.root_id = t.root_id AND o.id = t.observable_id
                                  WHERE t.root_id = '{root}' AND t.module IN ({names})
                                    AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT FROM analysis.results r WHERE r.root_id = t.root_id
                                                    AND r.observable_id = t.observable_id
                                                    AND r.module = t.module)"""):
            work[(path, m, o)] = (None, None, value)
    return work


HEX = re.compile(r"\b[0-9a-f]{32,128}\b")


def stable(text):
    """A normal form with each file named by its paths rather than its sha256, and each of its hashes
    (file_hash_analyzer's) by the same name, so two runs whose files' bytes differ (ExifTool's times,
    Ghostscript's rewrite) still line up, as JSON pointers to each leaf."""
    form = json.loads(text)
    names = {}
    shas = {}
    for key, observable in form["observables"].items():
        if not key.startswith("file:"):
            continue
        name = "file@" + "|".join(sorted(observable.get("paths", {})))
        names[key[len("file:"):]] = name
        shas[name] = key[len("file:"):]
        hashes = observable.get("results", {}).get("file_hash_analyzer", {}).get("details", {})
        for kind, value in (hashes.items() if isinstance(hashes, dict) else []):
            if isinstance(value, str) and HEX.fullmatch(value):
                names.setdefault(value, f"{name}#{kind}")
    form = json.loads(HEX.sub(lambda m: names.get(m.group(0), m.group(0)), text))
    leaves = {}

    def walk(value, pointer):
        if isinstance(value, dict) and value:
            for key, item in value.items():
                walk(item, f"{pointer}/{key}")
        elif isinstance(value, list) and value:
            for index, item in enumerate(value):
                walk(item, f"{pointer}/{index}")
        else:
            leaves[pointer] = value

    walk(form, "")
    return leaves, shas


def check_cache(failures):
    """The two-run check (docs/decisions/0004): with the cache on, CACHE_SAMPLES run twice. Every result
    of a cacheable module the first run kept, which is each one without an error, has to come from the
    cache the second time, with no task of it run in a pool; what the first run couldn't keep (a result
    with an error, a task that ended with none) runs again, as in ace3; and each sample's normal form
    is the same both times wherever a control run without the cache agrees with the first."""

    def expect(ok, message):
        log(("ok    " if ok else "FAIL  ") + message)
        if not ok:
            failures.append(f"the analysis cache: {message}")

    site = WORK / "site-cache"
    shutil.rmtree(site, ignore_errors=True)
    shutil.copytree(SITE, site)
    overlay = (site / "overlay.yaml").read_text()
    off = "analysis_cache:\n  enabled: false\n"
    tagger = "  site_tagger:\n    settings:\n"
    if off not in overlay or tagger not in overlay:
        expect(False, "the site's overlay turns the cache off and has a site_tagger section, as this check expects")
        return
    overlay = overlay.replace(off, "analysis_cache:\n  enabled: true\n")
    overlay = overlay.replace(tagger, "  site_tagger:\n    cache_ttl: 3600\n    settings:\n")
    (site / "overlay.yaml").write_text(overlay)
    sql("TRUNCATE cache.results, cache.probes")
    # the control: a run with the cache off, as the comparison runs, which says where two runs of a
    # sample differ without the cache (ExifTool's file times and what follows from them,
    # Ghostscript's rewrite of a PDF)
    control = run_samples(CACHE_SAMPLES)
    use_site(site)
    try:
        first = run_samples(CACHE_SAMPLES)
        kept = int(sql("SELECT count(*) FROM cache.results")[0][0])
        before = cacheable_work(first)
        second = run_samples(CACHE_SAMPLES)
        after = cacheable_work(second)
        keepable = {k for k, v in before.items() if v[0] is False}
        # an input whose bytes the second run made anew is another input, and misses
        same = {k for k in keepable if k in after and after[k][2] == before[k][2]}
        for module in CACHED_MODULES:
            mine = [k for k in same if k[1] == module]
            hits = [k for k in mine if after[k][1]]
            expect(mine and len(hits) == len(mine),
                   f"{module}: the second run took {len(hits)} of the {len(mine)} results the first kept "
                   "from the cache, for the same inputs")
        lost = sorted(k for k in same if not after[k][1])
        expect(not lost, f"no result the first run kept was made again for the same input: {lost}")
        anew = sorted(k for k in keepable - same)
        log(f"      {len(anew)} kept results were on files whose bytes the second run made anew, as "
            f"Ghostscript's rewrite's are, so missed: {[k[2] for k in anew]}")
        again = sorted(k for k, v in after.items() if not v[1])
        expect(all(k not in same for k in again),
               f"what ran again in a pool is what the first run couldn't keep, or a new input: "
               f"{len(again)} ({sorted({k[1] for k in again})})")
        ids = ", ".join(f"'{root}'" for _, root, _ in second)
        at_lease = sql(f"""SELECT count(*) FROM queue.tasks t JOIN analysis.results r
                           ON r.root_id = t.root_id AND r.observable_id = t.observable_id
                          AND r.module = t.module
                         WHERE r.cached_at IS NOT NULL AND t.root_id IN ({ids})""")[0][0]
        hits = sum(1 for v in after.values() if v[1])
        log(f"      the first run kept {kept} results; the second took {hits} from the cache, "
            f"{at_lease} of them at the task's lease and the rest where the task would have been queued")
        # wherever two runs without the cache agree, the run from the cache agrees too
        for (path, _, off), (_, _, form), (_, _, again_form) in zip(control, first, second):
            (off, off_shas), (cold, cold_shas), (warm, warm_shas) = (
                stable(off), stable(form), stable(again_form))
            # files whose bytes change from run to run, and a value that names one, as a redirection
            # chosen between two files by their sha256s does
            changing = {name for name in cold_shas
                        if {off_shas.get(name), warm_shas.get(name)} != {cold_shas[name]}}

            def run_dependent(value):
                return isinstance(value, str) and any(
                    value.removeprefix("file:").startswith(name) for name in changing)

            unstable = {p for p in off.keys() | cold.keys() if off.get(p) != cold.get(p)}
            moved = sorted(p for p in cold.keys() | warm.keys()
                           if cold.get(p) != warm.get(p) and p not in unstable
                           and not run_dependent(cold.get(p)) and not run_dependent(warm.get(p)))
            if moved:
                (WORK / f"cache-{Path(path).name}-first.json").write_text(form)
                (WORK / f"cache-{Path(path).name}-second.json").write_text(again_form)
            expect(not moved,
                   f"{path}'s normal form from the cache is the same as from a run, but for the "
                   f"{len(unstable)} values two runs without the cache differ in and what names a file "
                   f"whose bytes change every run ({len(changing)}): {moved[:5]}")
        check_phishkit_cache(expect)
    finally:
        use_site(SITE)


def check_phishkit_cache(expect):
    """phishkit_analyzer's results are kept (PLAN.md decision 27): with the cache on, the scanner
    check's page rendered twice gives the second root the first's result from the cache, with its
    files at the same paths and no scan of its own."""
    page = SCANNER_PAGE.read_bytes()
    roots = []
    for _ in range(2):
        root = submit_file(page, "phishkit_page.htm", "correlation", ["type=email.attachment"])
        wait_for(f"root {root} to finish", lambda: completed_after(root) is not None, within=240)
        roots.append(root)
    first, second = roots

    def result(root):
        return sql(f"""SELECT r.cached_at IS NOT NULL, coalesce(r.error, ''),
                             jsonb_array_length(r.details->'output_files')
                      FROM analysis.results r
                      WHERE r.root_id = '{root}' AND r.module = 'phishkit_analyzer'""")

    def scans(root):
        return sql(f"SELECT count(*) FROM queue.scans WHERE root_id = '{root}' AND scanner = 'phishkit'")[0][0]

    def files(root):
        return sorted(row[0] for row in sql(
            f"SELECT path FROM analysis.files WHERE root_id = '{root}' AND path LIKE 'phishkit/%'"))

    kept = sql("SELECT count(*) FROM cache.results WHERE module = 'phishkit_analyzer'")[0][0]
    image = sql("""SELECT probes->>'scanner:phishkit' FROM cache.probes
                    WHERE module = 'phishkit_analyzer'""")
    expect(result(first)[:1] and result(first)[0][:2] == ["f", ""] and scans(first) == "1"
           and kept == "1" and image and (image[0][0] or "").startswith("sha256:"),
           f"phishkit_analyzer's first render ran its scan and was kept under its image: "
           f"{result(first)}, {scans(first)} scan, {kept} kept, image {image}")
    expect(result(second)[:1] and result(second)[0][0] == "t" and scans(second) == "0"
           and files(second) == files(first) and files(first),
           f"phishkit_analyzer's second render came from the cache, with no scan and the same "
           f"files: {result(second)}, {scans(second)} scans, {len(files(second))} of "
           f"{len(files(first))} files")


def jobs_of(argv):
    """The number after --jobs, or None without it, which leaves it to `ace compare`."""
    if "--jobs" not in argv:
        return None
    following = argv[argv.index("--jobs") + 1:]
    if not following or not following[0].isdigit() or int(following[0]) < 1:
        raise SystemExit("e2e: --jobs takes a number, 1 or more")
    return int(following[0])


CHECKS = ["gui", "command", "email", "search", "ai", "lists", "scanners", "browser", "library-diff",
          "inventory", "compare", "cache"]
SELECTIONS = ["--samples", "--modules", "--crates", "--changed"]


def value_of(argv, name):
    """The comma-separated values after `name`, or None without it."""
    if name not in argv:
        return None
    following = argv[argv.index(name) + 1:]
    if not following or following[0].startswith("--"):
        raise SystemExit(f"e2e: {name} takes a comma-separated list")
    return [v for v in following[0].split(",") if v]


def checks_of(argv):
    """The checks --only names, with what each needs, or every check without it."""
    named = value_of(argv, "--only")
    if named is None:
        return set(CHECKS)
    if named == ["none"]:
        named = []
    unknown = [c for c in named if c not in CHECKS]
    if unknown:
        raise SystemExit(f"e2e: --only names no such check: {', '.join(unknown)}; the checks are "
                         + ", ".join(CHECKS))
    checks = set(named)
    if checks & {"search", "ai"}:
        checks.add("email")
    if "cache" in checks:
        checks.add("compare")
    return checks


def crates_changed():
    """The crates with uncommitted changes in this checkout, staged or not, untracked files too."""
    if not (ROOT / ".git").exists():
        raise SystemExit(f"e2e: --changed needs a git checkout, and {ROOT} isn't one")
    out = subprocess.run(
        ["git", "-C", str(ROOT), "status", "--porcelain", "--untracked-files=all", "--", "crates"],
        check=True, capture_output=True, text=True,
    ).stdout
    return sorted({line[3:].split(" -> ")[-1].split("/")[1] for line in out.splitlines()})


def modules_of_crates(crates):
    """The modules docs/modules.md's inventory says each crate holds, by its third column."""
    held = {}
    for line in (ROOT / "docs" / "modules.md").read_text().splitlines():
        cells = [c.strip().strip("`") for c in line.strip().strip("|").split("|")]
        if len(cells) > 3 and cells[2].startswith("ace-mod-") and re.fullmatch(r"[a-z0-9_]+", cells[0]):
            held.setdefault(cells[2], set()).add(cells[0])
    missing = [c for c in crates if c not in held]
    if missing:
        raise SystemExit(f"e2e: docs/modules.md names no module in {', '.join(missing)}")
    return sorted(set().union(*(held[c] for c in crates))) if crates else []


def samples_with_modules(paths, modules):
    """The samples where ace3's tree has a result of one of the modules, or where the last report
    found a difference in one."""
    wanted = set(modules)
    chosen = set()
    for path in paths:
        tree = TREES / "reference" / f"{path}.json"
        if tree.is_file():
            observables = json.loads(tree.read_text()).get("observables") or {}
            if any(wanted & set(o.get("results") or {}) for o in observables.values()):
                chosen.add(path)
    last = WORK / "compare" / "report.json"
    if last.is_file():
        for sample in json.loads(last.read_text()).get("samples", []):
            if wanted & set(sample.get("modules") or {}):
                chosen.add(sample["sample"])
    return [p for p in paths if p in chosen]


def samples_of(argv):
    """The samples a selection names, in the manifest's order: None without a selection, which is
    the whole sample set, and possibly none."""
    given = [name for name in SELECTIONS if name in argv]
    if not given:
        return None
    if len(given) > 1:
        raise SystemExit(f"e2e: {' and '.join(given)} can't be given together")
    paths = [s["path"] for s in json.loads((ROOT / "samples" / "manifest.json").read_text())["samples"]]
    if "--samples" in argv:
        globs = value_of(argv, "--samples")
        chosen = [p for p in paths if any(fnmatch.fnmatchcase(p, g) for g in globs)]
        log(f"comparing the {len(chosen)} samples matching {', '.join(globs)}")
        return chosen
    if "--modules" in argv:
        modules = value_of(argv, "--modules")
    elif "--crates" in argv:
        modules = modules_of_crates(value_of(argv, "--crates"))
    else:
        crates = crates_changed()
        others = [c for c in crates if not c.startswith("ace-mod-")]
        if others:
            log(f"comparing the whole sample set: {', '.join(others)} changed, and no module's crate "
                "says which samples those reach")
            return None
        if not crates:
            log("comparing no sample: no crate has an uncommitted change")
            return []
        modules = modules_of_crates(crates)
        log(f"changed: {', '.join(crates)}")
    chosen = samples_with_modules(paths, modules)
    log(f"comparing the {len(chosen)} samples that reach {', '.join(modules)}")
    return chosen


def threshold_over(samples):
    """docs/acceptance.md's threshold over a selection of samples, from the report `ace compare`
    wrote: no unexplained difference, no failed sample and, outside CI, no absent one. Returns why
    it isn't met, or an empty list."""
    report = json.loads((WORK / "compare" / "report.json").read_text())
    unmet = []
    if report["totals"]["unexplained"]:
        unmet.append(f"{report['totals']['unexplained']} unexplained differences")
    if report["failed"]:
        unmet.append(f"{len(report['failed'])} samples failed")
    if report["absent"] and not os.environ.get("CI"):
        unmet.append(f"{len(report['absent'])} samples are absent")
    log(f"the threshold over the {len(samples)} samples compared; a row of differences.md that "
        "matched nothing isn't checked, since the samples it covers may not have run")
    return unmet


# The audit of the modules' declarations of what they take (PLAN.md decision 23, ace_core::takes):
# with ACE_RS_TAKES_AUDIT=1 in the environment (a site's prefix in place of ACE_RS_) the stack's core
# queues every task and marks the ones a declaration would have declined. This is
# ace_core::takes::audit_report's query.
TAKES_AUDIT = os.environ.get(PREFIX + "TAKES_AUDIT", "") in ("1", "true")
LOST_TASKS = """
SELECT t.id, t.module, o.type || ':' || o.value, t.declined,
       CASE WHEN r.id IS NOT NULL THEN 'result' ELSE 'failed' END
FROM queue.tasks t
JOIN analysis.observables o ON o.root_id = t.root_id AND o.id = t.observable_id
LEFT JOIN analysis.results r ON r.root_id = t.root_id
     AND r.observable_id = t.observable_id AND r.module = t.module
WHERE t.declined IS NOT NULL AND (r.id IS NOT NULL OR t.state = 'failed')
ORDER BY t.id
"""


def check_takes_audit(failures):
    """Under ACE_RS_TAKES_AUDIT, that no task a declaration declined stored a result or failed. The
    marked tasks by module, and any such task, go to <work>/takes-audit.txt."""
    if not TAKES_AUDIT:
        return
    marked = sql("SELECT module, count(*), count(*) FILTER (WHERE state = 'done') FROM queue.tasks "
                 "WHERE declined IS NOT NULL GROUP BY module ORDER BY count(*) DESC, module")
    total = sql("SELECT count(*), count(*) FILTER (WHERE declined IS NOT NULL) FROM queue.tasks")[0]
    lost = sql(LOST_TASKS)
    lines = [f"{total[1]} of {total[0]} tasks marked as declined by their module's declaration",
             *(f"  {count:>7} {module} ({done} done)" for module, count, done in marked),
             f"{len(lost)} marked tasks stored a result or failed",
             *("  " + "\t".join(row) for row in lost)]
    (WORK / "takes-audit.txt").write_text("\n".join(lines) + "\n")
    if lost:
        log(f"FAIL  {len(lost)} tasks a module's declaration declined stored a result or failed; "
            f"see {WORK / 'takes-audit.txt'}")
        failures.append("the audit of the modules' declarations found tasks they would lose")
    else:
        log(f"ok    the audit: {total[1]} of {total[0]} tasks marked as declined, and none of them "
            f"stored a result or failed")


def compare_with_ace3(threshold=False, jobs=None, samples=None):
    """Runs `ace compare` over the sample set, or the given samples, in a one-off ace container, with
    the report under <work>/compare, `jobs` samples at once when it's given. Returns its exit code,
    and over a selection of samples 1 when threshold_over says the threshold isn't met."""
    report = WORK / "compare"
    report.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    # ace3's trees were made against an empty brocess (tools/ace3/trees/brocess.json), and the
    # email logger has recorded this test's email by now
    sql("TRUNCATE brocess.smtplog, brocess.email_thread_message, brocess.email_thread_domain")
    # and with tools/ace3/trees/nrd.json's newly registered domains, as the core's list
    domains = json.loads((TREES / "nrd.json").read_text())["domains"]
    sql("TRUNCATE nrd.domains; INSERT INTO nrd.domains (domain) VALUES "
        + ", ".join("('" + d.replace("'", "''") + "')" for d in domains)
        + " ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING")
    # and with tools/ace3/trees' detections, tags and site tags (PLAN.md 7.6)
    problem = give_ace_rs_the_trees_world()
    if problem:
        log(f"FAIL  the tagging and detection modules' world: {problem}")
        return 1
    log("ok    ace-rs has the detections, tags and site tags ace3's trees were made with")
    # the recorded Splunk job counts requests from when the responder started
    compose("restart", "responder")
    compose("up", "-d", "--wait", "responder")
    command = [
        "run", "--rm", "--no-deps", "--user", f"{os.getuid()}:{os.getgid()}", "-e", "ACE_RS_API_KEY",
        "-v", f"{ROOT / 'samples'}:/compare/samples:ro",
        "-v", f"{TREES}:/compare/trees:ro",
        "-v", f"{report}:/compare/report",
        "ace", ACE_COMMAND, "compare", "--samples", "/compare/samples", "--trees", "/compare/trees",
        "--report", "/compare/report",
    ]
    if jobs:
        command += ["--jobs", str(jobs)]
    for sample in samples or ():
        command += ["--only", sample]
    if threshold and samples is None:
        command.append("--threshold")
        if os.environ.get("CI"):
            command.append("--allow-absent")
    code = compose(*command, check=False, exit_code=True)
    log(f"the comparison's report is in {report}")
    if threshold and samples is not None and code == 0:
        unmet = threshold_over(samples)
        for reason in unmet:
            log(f"FAIL  {reason}")
        code = 1 if unmet else 0
    return code


def run(email, kill, failures):
    """Submits the email and waits for its root to complete. With kill, freezes the parser pool
    first, kills it once it holds a lease, and starts it again. Returns the root and seconds to
    completion."""
    # the recorded Splunk job answers "running" twice and then "done", counting requests from
    # when the responder started, so each run starts it again to see the same answers
    compose("restart", "responder")
    compose("up", "-d", "--wait", "responder")
    if kill:
        compose("pause", "parsers")
    # as ace3's email collectors mark the email they collected, so the email logger takes it
    original = {"type": "file", "value": hashlib.sha256(email).hexdigest(),
                "directives": ["original_email"]}
    root = submit(email, observables=[original])
    log(f"submitted root {root}{' with the parser pool frozen' if kill else ''}")
    if kill:
        held = wait_for(
            "the frozen parser pool to be given a task",
            lambda: sql(
                f"""SELECT module, lease_owner FROM queue.tasks WHERE root_id = '{root}'
                    AND state = 'running' AND lease_owner LIKE 'parsers/%'"""
            ),
            within=30,
        )
        log(f"the frozen parser pool holds {held}; killing it with SIGKILL")
        compose("kill", "-s", "SIGKILL", "parsers")
        killed_at = time.monotonic()
        compose("up", "-d", "--wait", "parsers")
        log(f"started the parser pool again {time.monotonic() - killed_at:.1f}s after the kill")
    seconds = wait_for(f"root {root} to complete", lambda: completed_after(root), within=300)
    log(f"root {root} completed {seconds:.2f}s after it was created")
    for row in tasks(root):
        log("  task " + " | ".join(row))
    check_root(root, failures)
    if kill:
        # the task the frozen pool held when it was killed, whichever parser module it was
        held_modules = {module for module, _ in held}
        taken_back = [r for r in tasks(root) if r[0] in held_modules and int(r[4]) >= 2]
        ok = bool(taken_back) and all(r[3] == "done" for r in taken_back)
        log(("ok    " if ok else "FAIL  ")
            + f"the killed pool's task ran again and ended done: {taken_back}")
        if not ok:
            failures.append(f"{root}: the killed pool's task didn't run again")
    return root, seconds


def finish(failures):
    if failures:
        log(f"{len(failures)} check(s) failed:")
        for failure in failures:
            log(f"  {failure}")
        return 1
    log("every check passed")
    return 0


def main(argv):
    if CACHE and not COMPARE:
        raise SystemExit("e2e: ACE_RS_E2E_CACHE needs ACE_RS_E2E_COMPARE: the cache's check runs in the "
                         "world the comparison sets up")
    keep = "--keep" in argv
    compare_only = "--compare" in argv
    jobs = jobs_of(argv) or POOL_SLOTS
    checks = checks_of(argv)
    samples = samples_of(argv)
    if samples is not None:
        # a selection alone compares those samples and checks nothing else
        checks = checks | {"compare"} if "--only" in argv else {"compare"}
    if checks != set(CHECKS):
        log(f"checks: {', '.join(c for c in CHECKS if c in checks) or 'none'}")
    WORK.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    commit = make_signatures()
    log(f"signatures at {WORK / 'signatures'}, commit {commit}")
    browser = has_browser()
    if not browser and "ACE_RS_E2E_COMPOSE" not in os.environ:
        raise SystemExit("e2e: compose.yaml has no browser service")
    build_scanner_images()
    build = [] if "--no-build" in argv else ["--build"]
    compose("up", "-d", *build, "--wait", *SERVICES, *(["browser"] if browser else []))
    failures = []
    try:
        make_key()
        wait_for(
            "the core to build the fixture's ruleset",
            lambda: sql(f"SELECT 1 FROM yara.rulesets WHERE commit = '{commit}'"),
            within=120,
        )
        wait_for(
            "the parser pool to load it",
            lambda: "the first ruleset loaded" in compose("logs", "parsers", capture=True),
            within=60,
        )
        if compare_only:
            if samples == []:
                log("no sample to compare")
            elif compare_with_ace3(jobs=jobs, samples=samples) != 0:
                failures.append("ace compare couldn't run every sample; see above")
            check_takes_audit(failures)
            return finish(failures)
        if "gui" in checks:
            check_gui(failures)
        make_analyst()
        if "command" in checks:
            check_gui_command(failures)
        email = (ROOT / "samples" / SAMPLE).read_bytes()
        if "email" in checks:
            first, undisturbed = run(email, kill=False, failures=failures)
            second, killed = run(email, kill=True, failures=failures)
            log(f"completion: {undisturbed:.2f}s undisturbed, {killed:.2f}s with the parser pool "
                f"killed mid-run (lease {LEASE_SECONDS}s)")
            if killed <= undisturbed:
                failures.append("the run with the kill wasn't slower; did the kill land?")
            form = normal_form(first)
            (WORK / "normal-form.json").write_text(form)
            check_normal_form(form, failures)
            killed_form = normal_form(second)
            (WORK / "normal-form-killed.json").write_text(killed_form)
            if form == killed_form:
                log("ok    both roots have the same normal form, killed pool and all")
            else:
                log("FAIL  the roots' normal forms differ; see normal-form*.json in " + str(WORK))
                failures.append("the same email's two roots have different normal forms")
            check_root_metrics([first, second], failures)
        if "search" in checks:
            check_search(first, second, failures)
        if "ai" in checks:
            check_ai(first, failures)
        if "lists" in checks:
            check_list_edit(email, failures)
        if "scanners" in checks:
            check_scanners(failures)
        if "browser" not in checks:
            pass
        elif browser:
            try:
                check_live_alert(email, failures)
            except SystemExit as error:
                log(f"FAIL  the browser test: {error}")
                failures.append(f"the browser test: {error}")
        else:
            log("SKIP  the browser test: the Compose file has no browser service")
        if not SITE_RUN and "library-diff" in checks:
            check_library_diff(failures)
        if not SITE_RUN and "inventory" in checks:
            check_module_inventory(failures)
        # a selection of samples is a request to compare them, in a site's run too
        if (COMPARE or samples is not None) and "compare" in checks and samples != []:
            compare_failed = compare_with_ace3(threshold=True, jobs=jobs, samples=samples) != 0
            if samples is None:
                check_ports_compared(failures)
            check_takes_audit(failures)
            if compare_failed:
                failures.append("the acceptance threshold (docs/acceptance.md) isn't met; see "
                                "above and target/e2e/compare/report.md")
            elif samples is None:
                log("ok    the acceptance threshold is met: every difference from ace3 is listed "
                    "in differences.md, and every row matched one")
            else:
                log(f"ok    the acceptance threshold is met over the {len(samples)} samples compared")
        elif samples == []:
            log("SKIP  the comparison: no sample selected")
        if CACHE and "cache" in checks and samples != []:
            check_cache(failures)
    finally:
        if failures or keep:
            for service in ("ace", "parsers", "sandbox", "lookups", "scanners", "responder",
                            *(["browser"] if browser else [])):
                print(f"----- {service} logs (last 40 lines)")
                print(compose("logs", "--no-color", "--tail", "40", service, capture=True,
                              check=False))
        if not keep:
            compose("down", "-v", "--remove-orphans", check=False)
    return finish(failures)


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))
